add the string row and its narrowing and fix the doc comment.\n7|P3 — one row each for items a, b, e, f, g (the reviewer marks these cheap and says they close real gaps); state the P3-i bound; union the 10.2 acceptance cases (P3-j); relabel the two non-narrowing rows (P3-k).\n8|Finally: re-run the battery twice on the final tree, re-run tracecheck, and report the ratio you MEASURE. Keep the candidate UNCOMMITTED.\n9|Procedure: your Story branch has already been refreshed onto c3aae73 and descends from it — do not refresh again unless origin/main actually moves. This is the FINAL leaf, so internal/traceability IS yours: the registry is `internal/traceability/ownership.v0.7.0.json` (the adopted one), the pin must be re-derived from the registry as it stands in your candidate, and the README \"Measured coverage of this repository\" subsection must equal what tracecheck prints on your tree and must still pass the landed `readme_coverage_pin_test.go` closed spelled-number map. Never commit on the Story branch, never edit `.task-board` directly, never self-accept. Re-run the full configured validation suite once (30 commands; read the count from the candidate config; command 5 is the race gate with `-timeout 25m` and can take 25-40 minutes under concurrent runs) — and run your own package tests BEFORE handoff; construction is not your first test run. Update the results with a finding-by-finding table (finding -> change -> the test that fails without it -> evidence path), update the conformance matrix and the evidence archive (a real gzip archive, one raw log per plant with its subprocess exit, PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1), re-complete the checklist, then `task-board handoff TASK-260830-32ypr2 --role developer` so revision 2 is constructed, and exit promptly. Hand off no later than 3 hours in.\n10|PARTIAL-ATTEMPT RECOVERY: if a previous attempt died mid-way, the Story worktree still carries its partial edits — start with `git -C .temp/STORY-260830-1cyj0q/worktree status --short` and `git diff`, state what you inherited, and verify it against this brief instead of assuming it is correct.\n11|Canonical CLI /Users/iv/.curator/global/bin/task-board. Model: muse-spark max. The same claude-opus-5 max reviewer contract applies to revision 2.","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"read_file","outcome":"success"}}}
