{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c53b","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0b3c6-628c-70a3-ad39-75274b1adfea"},"sequence":248,"recorded_at":1780531400000491,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"94f324ce-ad7a-4eb7-9c54-86bfc93d2b24","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"94f324ce-ad7a-4eb7-9c54-86bfc93d2b24","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"94f324ce-ad7a-4eb7-9c54-86bfc93d2b24"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0b3c7-02ed-7941-b27f-a4a5fd222b84"},"task_id":"01a0b3c7-02ed-7941-b27f-a4a5fd222b84","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a0b3c7-02ed-7941-b27f-a4a5fd222b84","chunk":"Read text file `/tmp/t32ypr2/verdict-rev1.md`.\n1|# TASK-260830-32ypr2 — Review verdict, Change Request revision 1\n2|\n3|Reviewer run: RUN-260918-320878 (claude-opus-5 max, reviewer/reviewer).\n4|Change Request: `CR-TASK-260830-32ypr2-1` revision 1 (story_final), base\n5|`c3aae73df906df1b5aa962c7bc3c16437dd920fa` (= `origin/main`), candidate tree\n6|`471e8282d6a8a31a7532ee7f0b5a9294b5dc15ca` (65 paths; patch sha256\n7|`566deda598876d35fb4ea5aa699966723a6f2fee3c1efb1141615c51f03ccba4`, verified\n8|byte-equal to `git diff c3aae73 471e828`). The live Story worktree's\n9|temp-index tree OID (`git add -A` into a scratch index copy) equalled\n10|`471e828…` before this review and `git status` stayed ` M LOGBOOK.md`,\n11|` M README.md`, ` M internal/traceability/{6 files}`, `?? internal/cloneproject/`\n12|throughout; worktree, index, branch and HEAD were never touched. Authority:\n13|`internal/specdoc/SPEC.v0.7.0.md` §13.14.1 (10331–10546), §10.2 (4851–4903),\n14|§7.8 (3738–3924), §1.6 common data model (line 324: \"Decoders MUST reject\n15|lone surrogate code points before canonicalization\").\n16|\n17|Method: isolated immutable copies of the exact candidate tree (`git archive\n18|471e828…` → `.temp/TASK-260830-32ypr2/review-rev1/{candidate,pristine}` plus\n19|`trunk` from `c3aae73`, the tracked `.task-board/.resources` and `.activity`\n20|dropped from all copies); `diff -rq` clean against `pristine` after every\n21|probe and battery; `PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1` on every harness, zero\n22|`__pycache__`/`.pyc` after the runs. Every probe in this verdict was executed\n23|on the candidate copy; the logs are in\n24|`TASK-260830-32ypr2_review-evidence-rev1.tar.gz`.\n25|\n26|## Verdict: CHANGES REQUESTED → `to-dev`\n27|\n28|One P1, three P2, and a P3 list. The technical body is mostly right and the\n29|producer's evidence reproduces: the 25-test package suite, the 49-row battery\n30|(49 KILLED + control SURVIVED, 2/2 in my runs), tracecheck at the quoted\n31|ratios, the re-derived registry digest, and the whole 41-package suite are\n32|all green on the exact candidate tree. What fails is (a) a live admit hole at\n33|this leaf's own entry — the fixture-native decoder forks the landed strict\n34|JSON gate and REWRITES source text while stamping `exact`, which is the P3-ζ\n35|class the predecessor's verdict deferred to this leaf by name; (b) the seven\n36|inherited-advisory groups are not mentioned anywhere in the results, matrix,\n37|TRACEABILITY or LOGBOOK (silently dropped, including production prose on the\n38|story_final patch that now states the final leaf did something it did not);\n39|(c) a §7.8 registry binding that discharges the 8 MiB adapter-frame clause\n40|with a test that constructs no frame, published in the README as\n41|\"Section 7.8 at 2/2, bound to internal/cloneproject\".\n42|\n43|## Section 0 — Inherited advisories from TASK-260830-2g5be6 rev3 (the accepted predecessor verdict)\n44|\n45|The predecessor verdict carried seven advisory groups forward \"for the\n46|Story's FINAL leaf TASK-260830-32ypr2 or a follow-up on internal/clonesnap\"\n47|and asked for a recorded decision on each. The leaf's own delta\n48|(`git diff --stat 3005d78 471e828`) touches no file under\n49|`internal/clonesnap` or `internal/clonebundle`, and\n50|`grep -i -E \"P3|advis|AfterWalk|chmod|BuildAdmissionReceipt|empty-cwd|lone.surrogate|EncodeNativeIdentity|swaps-pre-post|quiet\"`\n51|over `TASK-260830-32ypr2_results.md` and `_conformance-matrix.md` returns\n52|nothing.\n53|\n54|| # | Advisory (2g5be6 rev3) | Grade on this CR |\n55||---|---|---|\n56|| 1 | P3-a independent oracle for archive digests (`R3-archive-swaps-pre-post`) | SILENTLY DROPPED |\n57|| 2 | P3-b quiet-store row under `RaceArchive`+`OperatorExplicit` | SILENTLY DROPPED |\n58|| 3 | P3-c/d chmod-000 rows or restate the `walk.go` \"never an absence\" comment as a bound | SILENTLY DROPPED |\n59|| 4 | P3-e state the AfterWalk-seam bound in TRACEABILITY and results | SILENTLY DROPPED |\n60|| 5 | P3-f direct `BuildAdmissionReceipt(…, \"ultra\")` row or state the bound | SILENTLY DROPPED |\n61|| 6 | P3-g empty-cwd row; early-pass \"nothing installed\" row or reword | SILENTLY DROPPED |\n62|| 7a | P3-ζ lone surrogate at the text admission site — the tree itself says \"Deferred to the Final leaf, which owns projection fidelity over session/event text\" (`internal/clonesnap/TRACEABILITY.md:145-148`) | NOT CLOSED and LIVE at this leaf's entry: see P1-a |\n63|| 7b | P3-η remainder (`EncodeNativeIdentity` standalone contract) | SILENTLY DROPPED |\n64|| 7c | P3-ζ′ fidelity vocabulary spelled twice — the tree says \"The FINAL leaf unifies or exports one owner\" (`internal/clonesnap/project.go:41-43`, `TRACEABILITY.md:132-135`) | SILENTLY DROPPED; the production comment is now false prose on the story_final patch |\n65|\n66|An explicit deferral with an owner (a follow-up on `internal/clonesnap`) is\n67|an acceptable decision for 1–6 and 7b; 7a must be closed here (P1-a); 7c needs\n68|either the unification or a rewrite of the two sentences that promise it.\n69|\n70|## Findings\n71|\n72|### P1 — production admits and rewrites what it must refuse, at this leaf's entry, and stamps `exact`\n73|\n74|**P1-a `parseNativeLine`/`decodeBodyObject` fork the landed strict decoder;\n75|lone-surrogate escapes are rewritten to U+FFFD and duplicate members are\n76|guessed last-wins, both sealed with `capture_status: exact`.**\n77|`internal/cloneproject/native.go:73` and `:233` decode with plain\n78|`encoding/json` instead of the landed `environ.DecodeStrictObject`\n79|(`internal/environ/decode.go:54`, the single JSON entry the epic already\n80|converged sessadapter and dirnode onto; it refuses non-UTF-8, lone surrogate\n81|escapes, duplicate members and trailing data). Pristine candidate, real\n82|`clonesnap.Capture` → `Normalize` path (`logs/probes-pristine.log`):\n83|\n84|- PA: `{\"text\":\"\\ud800\"}` → ADMITTED `user_message`, sealed content bytes\n85|  `ef bf bd` (U+FFFD), `capture_status=exact`; same for `\\udc00`,\n86|  `A\\ud800B` (→ `A�B`), `\\ud800\\ud800`. The raw_ref resolves to the source\n87|  line carrying `\\ud800`; the canonical event carries different text.\n88|- PB: `\"native_event_id\":\"evt-\\ud800\"` → evidence `native_event_id=\"evt-�\"`\n89|  (the evidence identity itself is rewritten); `\"native_type\":\"frob\\ud800\"`\n90|  → `opaque_event` with `native_type=\"frob�\"`.\n91|- PC: `{\"text\":\"A\",\"text\":\"B\"}` → content `\"B\"`, `exact`;\n92|  `\"native_type\":\"frobnicate\",\"native_type\":\"message/user\"` → `user_message`\n93|  (an ambiguous record coerced into a known kind);\n94|  `\"protection\":\"encrypted\",\"protection\":\"none\"` on `reasoning/summary` →\n95|  `reasoning_summary` with the body text projected; `\"origin\":\"foreign\",\n96|  \"origin\":\"native\"` on an instruction → reaches the effective snapshot with\n97|  `authority=high`.\n98|\n99|Why P1: §1.6 line 324 is a MUST for decoders feeding canonicalization; the\n100|AC says opaque records are \"never dropped, guessed\"; the leaf's own\n101|TRACEABILITY row (`internal/cloneproject/TRACEABILITY.md:91`, \"1.6 text is\n102|valid UTF-8, never rewritten\") is false; and this is the exact class the\n103|predecessor deferred to this leaf (Section 0, 7a). It is also rejection\n104|shape (c) of the producer brief (a fork of a landed gate that diverges).\n105|The fix is not a forced fit — I applied it in a throwaway copy\n106|(`logs/fixprobe-strict-decode.log`): replacing both decodes with\n107|`environ.DecodeStrictObject` turns every PA/PB/PC admit into a refusal\n108|naming the fault (`lone surrogate escape`, `duplicate member in member\n109|text`), and the committed suite stays green except for the\n110|`malformed_json_line` fragment (keep \"is not a JSON object\" in the message).\n111|Ship: the delegation, one lone-surrogate row (text member and envelope\n112|member), one duplicate-member row per envelope/body site, and narrowing\n113|mutants that admit exactly one escape / exactly one duplicated member.\n114|\n115|### P2 — evidence, traceability and a second fork\n116|\n117|**P2-a Inherited advisories silently dropped (Section 0).** Nothing in the\n118|results, matrix, LOGBOOK or either TRACEABILITY records a decision for\n119|groups 1–6, 7b, 7c; 7a is live (P1-a). The story_final patch ships two\n120|production/traceability sentences promising work this leaf did not do\n121|(`internal/clonesnap/project.go:41-43`, `internal/clonesnap/TRACEABILITY.md:132-147`).\n122|Record a decision per group in the results (closed → the test; deferred →\n123|owner + reason), and either unify the fidelity vocabulary or rewrite the two\n124|sentences as a bound with the follow-up owner named.\n125|\n126|**P2-b `section:7.8` bound `full 2/2` to `internal/cloneproject` with a\n127|clause no test drives at the named site.** Registry\n128|`internal/traceability/ownership.v0.7.0.json:4735-4764`: production owner\n129|changed to `internal/cloneproject/normalize.go Normalize`; clause `7.8#1`\n130|(\"Large data is referenced by manifest or Blob Descriptor ID and MUST NOT be\n131|embedded in the 8 MiB frame\", spec 3785) is discharged by\n132|`clone-projection-fidelity` → `TestNormalizeInlineContentBoundary`, a test\n133|that constructs no adapter frame and never touches the 8 MiB bound; the\n134|64 KiB inline rule it does prove is §13.14.1's. The leaf's own matrix (D)\n135|and TRACEABILITY state \"§7.8 operation frames … NOT APPLICABLE here: wiring\n136|stays `sessadapter`\", and README:3258-3260 now publishes \"Section 7.8 at\n137|2/2, bound to internal/cloneproject\". The honest binding exists on trunk:\n138|`internal/sessadapter/protocol.go:34` (`MaxFrameBytes = 8 << 20`) with\n139|`TestDecodeRequestFrameRefusesOversizeFrame` and `TestFrameBoundEdges`\n140|(`internal/sessadapter/envelope_test.go:127,144`). Bind `7.8#1` to a\n141|sessadapter acceptance case over those tests with the production owner in\n142|sessadapter (or leave 7.8 `partial 1/2` with a gap), keep `7.8#2` on\n143|`session-adapter-call-binding` (that one is real: `CheckCallBinding`,\n144|`discovery_test.go:103,165`), re-derive the digest, update the pin tests and\n145|the README prose. `--section 7.8` admission must not be claimed by a\n146|projection test.\n147|\n148|**P2-c `bodyUint53` forks `environ.CheckUint53Bounds` and admits\n149|string-typed numbers.** `internal/cloneproject/native.go:278-296` decodes\n150|into `json.Number` and checks digits; a JSON string `\"5\"` is accepted by\n151|`encoding/json` into `json.Number`, so `{\"input_tokens\":\"5\",\"output_tokens\":0}`\n152|→ ADMITTED, ledger `SourceInputTokens:5` (PD, `logs/probes-pristine.log`).\n153|The doc comment says \"never a fraction, exponent, or string\" — false. The\n154|landed `rawUint53` refuses a string (`value.(json.Number)` on a string\n155|fails). Same class: `\"v\":\"1\"` is admitted as envelope version 1. Delegate to\n156|`environ.CheckUint53Bounds(raw, 0, maxUint53)` and add the string row plus a\n157|narrowing.\n158|\n159|### P3 — sub-members, axes and gates with no committed row (production correct in each case; each plant SURVIVED the whole committed suite 2/2 with its admitted behaviour executed under the plant, `logs/under-mutant/*.log`)\n160|\n161|- **P3-a Determinism is measured along one axis.** `R1-actors-unsorted`\n162|  (drop `sort.Strings(selectors)`, `dispatch.go:414`) SURVIVED 2/2; under it\n163|  a session with three extra actors sealed 3 distinct byte strings over 12\n164|  projections (`under-mutant/R1-actors-unsorted.log`); pristine 1. Matrix\n165|  row 22 says \"a proven property, not a gate … no plant required\" — the sort\n166|  IS the gate. One determinism row with ≥2 extra actors.\n167|- **P3-b type/protection agreement arm unrowed.**\n168|  `R2-reasoning-encrypted-admits-signed` (`dispatch.go:106-109`) SURVIVED\n169|  2/2: `reasoning/encrypted` declared `protection:signed` projects\n170|  `opaque_reasoning` with `foreign_signature_unverifiable` under the plant;\n171|  pristine refuses. One refusal row per arm.\n172|- **P3-c width edges unwitnessed.** `R3-directive-width-4097`\n173|  (`native.go` directive `> 4096`) and `R3b-call-id-width-513` (call_id\n174|  `> 512`) SURVIVED 2/2; the `N-string-bound` row is called \"representative\n175|  for the shared character-width rule\" but pins only `native_event_id`.\n176|  Same shape for `tool_name` (definition and call). Either witness each edge\n177|  or route all of them through one shared helper and pin that.\n178|- **P3-d trailing-bytes gate unrowed.** `R4-trailing-bytes-admitted`\n179|  (`native.go:79`) SURVIVED 2/2; under the plant `{…}x` projects\n180|  `user_message` with a range covering the `x`.\n181|- **P3-e protected non-reasoning tool records reach opaque only via the\n182|  fold-skip, which has no row.** `R5-protected-tools-folded`\n183|  (`normalize.go:351`) SURVIVED 2/2; under the plant a protected `tool/call`\n184|  REFUSES (\"unknown member ciphertext\") instead of projecting `opaque_event`\n185|  (pristine: `opaque_event`, the unprotected result becomes an aborted\n186|  orphan). `TestNormalizeProtectedMessageBecomesOpaqueEvent` pins the\n187|  message shape only.\n188|- **P3-f result status vocabulary unrowed.** `R6-result-status-pending`\n189|  (`native.go:476`) SURVIVED 2/2; under it `status:\"pending\"` is admitted\n190|  and the call resolves `completed` with `ResultStatus:pending`.\n191|- **P3-g size gate shadowed by a shared fragment.** `R7-size-check-skipped`\n192|  (`normalize.go:300`) SURVIVED 2/2: `tampered_blob` flips a byte at equal\n193|  size and asserts the fragment \"disagrees\", which both the size arm and the\n194|  digest arm emit; a one-extra-byte blob reaches the size arm on pristine\n195|  (`blob size 133 disagrees with raw count 132`) and the digest arm under the\n196|  plant. Assert the arm's own message and add the size-drift row.\n197|- **P3-h unknown+protected body refusal is pinned in neither direction.**\n198|  `R8-body-decode-unknown-protected-skipped` (`dispatch.go:102`) SURVIVED\n199|  2/2: pristine REFUSES `frobnicate`/`encrypted`/`{\"mystery\":true}` (\"body\n200|  carries unknown member\") — i.e. a wholly unknown record is refused because\n201|  its body is not `{ciphertext}` — while under the plant it projects\n202|  `opaque_event` with both reasons. That contradicts the doc's \"type-level\n203|  unknowns become opaque_event\". Decide (I would not decode the body of an\n204|  unknown type at all) and pin it.\n205|- **P3-i non-JSONL included members refuse the whole projection.** PI:\n206|  a 3-byte binary `durable_index_required` member and a text\n207|  `derived_cache_optional` member both refuse `Normalize` (\"is not a JSON\n208|  object\"). Every included non-`unknown` member is parsed as the JSONL log;\n209|  the doc's bound names only \"included durable capture members\". State the\n210|  bound explicitly (or parse `durable_payload` only and route the rest).\n211|- **P3-j `section:10.2` binding dropped eight landed acceptance-case\n212|  attributions** (`scalar-digest-validation`, …,\n213|  `localstore-immutable-blob-install`, `localstore-sqlite-projection`) when\n214|  it was rewritten; `localstore-immutable-blob-install` is the actual\n215|  fsync/verify/atomic-install owner of `10.2#2`. Union, do not replace.\n216|- **P3-k harness labels.** `N-empty-projection` (`< 0`) and\n217|  `N-overflow-truncate` (`if false {` around the install arm plus a\n218|  truncation) are not narrowings; the results say \"No row is an arm-delete\".\n219|  Label them (single-member class; behaviour swap) — both still measure what\n220|  the AC asks.\n221|- **P3-l `\"directives\":null` is admitted as zero directives** (PF); nit.\n222|\n223|## What is clean (verified, not read)\n224|\n225|1. **Invariant 1 (unknown → opaque):** rows 1–5 reproduce; `N-unknown-kind`,\n226|   `N-unknown-kind-wholly`, `N-unknown-member` KILLED 2/2 in my runs; raw\n227|   refs resolve through the real store layout; twice-projected bytes equal.\n228|2. **Invariant 2 (foreign reasoning opaque, instructions low, usage\n229|   source-only):** rows 6–10 reproduce, the forbidden-member sweeps hold,\n230|   `N-protection-encrypted`/`-signed`, `N-foreign-instruction`,\n231|   `N-foreign-payload-authority`, `N-usage-target` KILLED 2/2; a foreign\n232|   unprotected `reasoning/summary` projects `reasoning_summary`/`internal`\n233|   (allowed: only encrypted/signed must be opaque) and a protected known\n234|   `tool/call` projects `opaque_event` (PH).\n235|3. **Invariant 3 (tools inert):** the five-row matrix reproduces; live\n236|   surface empty in every row; `N-tool-incomplete`, `N-tool-orphan`,\n237|   `N-pending-aborted`, `N-pending-completed`, `N-callable`,\n238|   `N-callable-false`, `N-live-followup` KILLED 2/2.\n239|4. **Invariant 4 (shapes):** main-null parent, contiguous ordinals, parent\n240|   chain, single head; 65536 inline / 65537 blob-referenced and byte-exact;\n241|   multibyte bound measured in bytes on both sides (`clonebundle/event.go:736`\n242|   uses `len(text)` too; PG: 65538 bytes/21846 chars → blob, 65536\n243|   bytes/32768 chars → inline); `N-overflow-bound`, `N-overflow-truncate`,\n244|   `N-main-parent`, `N-parents-chain` KILLED 2/2.\n245|5. **Determinism/idempotency:** `TestNormalizeIsDeterministic` and the\n246|   shared-sink replay reproduce (blob count stable).\n247|6. **Story-close:** the edited registry is the adopted\n248|   `ownership.v0.7.0.json`; `git diff c3aae73 471e828` on it is additive plus\n249|   the two binding upgrades (trunk's 5 mesh-RPC cases and 3 upgraded bindings\n250|   intact); digest re-derived by zeroing the pin in a copy →\n251|   `69d156d99a3b13ae598c7de3152225eafe4576c8f33286e8e36f68f22235052a`\n252|   (`logs/digest-rederivation.log`), equal to the pin; `tracecheck` and\n253|   `--section 7.8`/`10.2` green with the quoted lines byte-equal\n254|   (`logs/tracecheck.log`, `section-*.log`); README fenced line byte-equal;\n255|   `TestREADMEMeasuredCoverageMatchesTracecheckReport` executed and PASS\n256|   (`logs/pkg-traceability-v.log`); LOGBOOK entry newest-first and purely\n257|   additive (`git diff c3aae73 471e828 -- LOGBOOK.md` has no deletions);\n258|   README deletions are only the rewritten coverage figures.\n259|7. **Hygiene:** CR paths ⊆ {LOGBOOK, README, clonebundle, cloneproject,\n260|   clonesnap, traceability}; `task-board.config.json` byte-identical to trunk\n261|   (30 commands); the 8 trunk-moved paths that intersect the CR carry only\n262|   additive/expected edits; gofmt 0 files, `go build`, `go vet`, linux and\n263|   windows builds, `cataloggen -adopted -check` all exit 0 on the copy.\n264|8. **Suite:** `go test ./... -count=1` 41/41 ok (2m31s,\n265|   `logs/cmd04-go-test-all.log`); `-race` on cloneproject, clonebundle,\n266|   clonesnap, traceability/... ok with no DATA RACE\n267|   (`logs/cmd05-race-story-packages.log`); cloneproject coverage 88.9%. The\n268|   remaining 37 packages' race lanes and fuzz gates are accepted from the CR\n269|   construction log (`required=30 green=30 failed=0`) and the producer's\n270|   `cmds/cmd05a-g` (41 ok, 0 DATA RACE) — not re-run by me.\n271|\n272|## Coverage ratio I measured\n273|\n274|24 of 24 producer matrix rows are driven through `Normalize` by a named\n275|committed test over `clonesnap.Capture` output (I re-ran all 62 PASS lines,\n276|`logs/pkg-cloneproject-v.log`). Of those, 21 are measured clean at the\n277|member level; row 5 (\"never dropped, guessed\") is contradicted on the\n278|duplicate-member axis (P1-a), row 22 (determinism) is measured on one axis\n279|only (P3-a), and rows 18/19/21 rest on stated clonebundle bounds for shape\n280|internals (acceptable, stated). Nine reviewer narrowings on unrowed gates\n281|SURVIVED 2/2 (P3-a..h) plus an applied control (`RC-control-comment`,\n282|SURVIVED); the producer's 49 rows KILLED 2/2 in my runs with the\n283|`C-doc-comment` control SURVIVED (`mutants/producer-run{1,2}-battery.log`,\n284|per-plant logs under `mutants/producer-run{1,2}/`).\n285|\n286|## Rework scope (for the producer)\n287|\n288|1. P1-a: delegate the envelope and body decodes to\n289|   `environ.DecodeStrictObject` (proven clean in `logs/fixprobe-strict-decode.log`);\n290|   add lone-surrogate rows (text member, envelope member) and duplicate-member\n291|   rows (envelope, body) with one narrowing each; fix TRACEABILITY row\n292|   \"never rewritten\" to name the gate that now enforces it.\n293|2. P2-a: a decision line per inherited advisory group (1–6, 7b, 7c) in the\n294|   results; rewrite `clonesnap/project.go:41-43` and\n295|   `clonesnap/TRACEABILITY.md:132-147` so they state what the tree does.\n296|3. P2-b: re-bind `7.8#1` to the sessadapter frame-bound tests with a\n297|   sessadapter production owner (or `partial 1/2` with a gap); re-derive the\n298|   digest, update `traceability_test.go`/`main_test.go`/README pins and prose.\n299|4. P2-c: `bodyUint53` → `environ.CheckUint53Bounds`; string row + narrowing;\n300|   fix the doc comment.\n301|5. P3: one row each for a–h (a, b, e, f, g are cheap and close real gaps);\n302|   state the P3-i bound; union the 10.2 acceptance cases (P3-j); relabel the\n303|   two non-narrowing rows (P3-k).\n304|6. Re-run the battery twice on the final tree, re-run tracecheck, and report\n305|   the measured ratio; keep the candidate UNCOMMITTED.","final_result":true}}}
