{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c67b","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0b3c6-628c-70a3-ad39-75274b1adfea"},"sequence":408,"recorded_at":1780531400000811,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"94f324ce-ad7a-4eb7-9c54-86bfc93d2b24","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"94f324ce-ad7a-4eb7-9c54-86bfc93d2b24","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"94f324ce-ad7a-4eb7-9c54-86bfc93d2b24"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0b3c7-6705-76e2-af36-a2fa7c945823"},"task_id":"01a0b3c7-6705-76e2-af36-a2fa7c945823","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a0b3c7-6705-76e2-af36-a2fa7c945823","chunk":"Read text file `internal/cloneproject/TRACEABILITY.md`.\n1|# Projection Fidelity Clause Coverage (TASK-260830-32ypr2)\n2|\n3|Owner: `internal/cloneproject`. Authority:\n4|`internal/specdoc/SPEC.v0.7.0.md`, Sections 7.8, 10.2, 13.14.1\n5|(the pinned sections are byte-identical to v0.6.0).\n6|This is the FINAL leaf's clause record for the projection-fidelity\n7|closure; the `internal/traceability` registry bindings and re-pin\n8|ship in this leaf as well (see the Story-close section below).\n9|\n10|## Why this package normalizes instead of clonebundle or clonesnap\n11|\n12|The first leaf (`internal/clonebundle`) owns the capture contracts:\n13|the closed manifest/boundary/session/event shapes, their builders\n14|and decoders. The second leaf (`internal/clonesnap`) owns the\n15|capture OPERATION over a real provider store. This package owns\n16|NORMALIZATION: deriving Canonical Sessions and Canonical Events\n17|from captured bytes. Every event and the session seal through the\n18|landed `clonebundle` builders (`BuildCanonicalEvent`,\n19|`BuildCanonicalSession`, `CheckOrdinalContiguity`,\n20|`RefuseUnstableForTarget`, `InstallRawBlob`) and re-decode through\n21|the landed decoders before return; overflow Blob Descriptors seal\n22|through `clonesnap.BuildBlobDescriptor`; no second manifest,\n23|session, event, blob, or identity model exists here.\n24|\n25|## Landed-owner reuse\n26|\n27|| Scope | Owner | Use |\n28||---|---|---|\n29|| Session/event/evidence shapes | `internal/clonebundle` | all Build/Decode/Check/Refuse entries above |\n30|| Overflow descriptor shape | `internal/clonesnap` | `BuildBlobDescriptor` (errors wrapped with the overflow cause) |\n31|| Blob install (no-replace, fsync, verify) | `internal/clonebundle` + `internal/localstore` | `InstallRawBlob`, `ObjectStore.PutBlob` |\n32|| Digests, UUIDv7, timestamps | `internal/scalar` | `ParseDigest`, `SHA256Digest`, `ParseUUIDv7` |\n33|| Character string measure | `internal/environ` | `StringLength` at every native bound |\n34|| Canonical bytes | `internal/canonicaljson` | `Canonicalize`, `CalculateObjectIdentity` (tests resolve overflow descriptors) |\n35|\n36|## Fixture-native per-kind payload fact registry\n37|\n38|Section 13.14.1 requires payloads to carry only their registered\n39|typed facts. The envelope and value model are landed (`checkPayload`\n40|in `clonebundle`); this package registers the exact facts it emits\n41|for each kind it projects. No other Canonical kind is emitted here.\n42|\n43|| Kind | Exact facts |\n44||---|---|\n45|| `user_message`, `assistant_message`, `reasoning_summary` | `content_blocks` (one `text` block, inline at or under 64 KiB, else `blob_descriptor_id` + `media_type`), `extensions` |\n46|| `opaque_reasoning` | `protection` (`encrypted`\\|`signed`), `byte_count`, `blob_descriptor_id`, `extensions` |\n47|| `opaque_event` (unknown record) | `native_type`, `byte_count`, `blob_descriptor_id`, `extensions` |\n48|| `opaque_event` (protected known record) | `native_type`, `protection`, `byte_count`, `blob_descriptor_id`, `extensions` |\n49|| `opaque_event` (unknown member) | `native_item_key`, `byte_count`, `blob_descriptor_id`, `extensions` |\n50|| `instruction_snapshot` | `authority` (`low` forced for foreign), `directives`, `extensions` |\n51|| `tool_definition_snapshot` | `tool_name`, `definition_digest`, `callable` (always false), `extensions` |\n52|| `tool_call` | `call_id`, `tool_name`, `resolution` (`completed`\\|`aborted`), `extensions` |\n53|| `tool_result` | `call_id`, `status` (`ok`\\|`error`), `resolution`, `extensions` |\n54|| `usage` | `input_tokens`, `output_tokens`, `extensions` |\n55|\n56|## Clause map\n57|\n58|| Pinned clause | Production entry | Test |\n59||---|---|---|\n60|| 13.14.1 unknown native records become raw-addressable opaque events | `Normalize`, `dispatchRecord` | `TestNormalizeUnknownRecordBecomesOpaqueEvent` (kind, `opaque` visibility, `unknown_native_event` reason, raw range resolves to the exact line) |\n61|| 13.14.1 almost-known records are never coerced into a neighbouring kind | `dispatchRecord` (exact type switch) | `TestNormalizeAlmostKnownRecordBecomesOpaqueEvent` (`message/smoke` stays `opaque_event`, never `user_message`) |\n62|| 13.14.1 unknown-class members become whole-member opaque events | `collectMembers` | `TestNormalizeUnknownMemberBecomesWholeMemberOpaque` (offset 0, full length, null native IDs, resolves to the whole member) |\n63|| 13.14.1 opaque events are never dropped, guessed, or re-typed | `Normalize` (deterministic order) | `TestNormalizeOpaqueIsStableAcrossProjections` (project twice, byte-identical, still `opaque_event`) |\n64|| 13.14.1 foreign encrypted reasoning is opaque-preserved | `dispatchProtected` | `TestNormalizeForeignEncryptedReasoningStaysOpaque` (`opaque_reasoning`, `foreign_encrypted_payload`, no content members, byte-exact round trip) |\n65|| 13.14.1 foreign signed reasoning is opaque-preserved | `dispatchProtected` | `TestNormalizeForeignSignedReasoningStaysOpaque` (`foreign_signature_unverifiable`, byte-exact) |\n66|| 13.14.1 native protected reasoning stays opaque with no foreign code | `dispatchProtected`, `cryptoReasons` | `TestNormalizeNativeProtectedReasoningStaysOpaque` (empty reasons) |\n67|| 13.14.1 protected known content never reaches a semantic kind | `dispatchProtected` | `TestNormalizeProtectedMessageBecomesOpaqueEvent` (encrypted assistant message is `opaque_event`) |\n68|| 13.14.1 unknown+protected records carry both stable reasons | `dispatchProtected` | `TestNormalizeUnknownProtectedRecordCarriesBothReasons` |\n69|| 13.14.1 foreign instructions are low-authority history | `dispatchInstruction`, `foldInstructions` | `TestNormalizeForeignInstructionCannotChangeEffectiveSnapshot` (effective snapshot native-only, foreign payload pins `low`), `TestNormalizeForeignOnlyInstructionLeavesSnapshotEmpty` |\n70|| 13.14.1 source usage is not target accounting | `foldUsage` | `TestNormalizeSourceUsageIsNotTargetAccounting` (source sums exact, target zero) |\n71|| 13.14.1 historical tools are inert; call+result resolves completed | `resolveToolCalls`, `deriveLiveSurface` | `TestNormalizeToolMatrix/call_with_result` (kinds, `internal` visibility, `completed`, empty live surface) |\n72|| 13.14.1 incomplete calls become aborted history and block pending action | `resolveToolCalls`, `deriveLiveSurface` | `TestNormalizeToolMatrix/call_without_result` (`aborted`, `unsafe_pending_action`, empty live surface), `TestNormalizeToolMatrix/result_without_call` (orphan `aborted`) |\n73|| 13.14.1 results arriving after the boundary complete the same call | `resolveToolCalls` over two captures | `TestNormalizeResultAfterBoundaryCompletes` (first capture `aborted`, second `completed`) |\n74|| 13.14.1 nested calls attribute to a parented subagent actor | `checkActors`, `buildResult` | `TestNormalizeToolMatrix/nested_subagent_call` (subagent actor, parent is main) |\n75|| 13.14.1 definitions never register a callable tool | `deriveLiveSurface`, `dispatchDefinition` | `TestNormalizeToolDefinitionNeverRegistersCallable` (`callable` false, `CallableTools` empty) |\n76|| 13.14.1 live surface stays empty over mixed history | `deriveLiveSurface` | `TestNormalizeLiveSurfaceStaysEmpty` |\n77|| 13.14.1 Canonical Session bounds (actors, ordered event IDs, head) | `buildResult` | `TestNormalizeSealsSessionShape` (ordinals, parent chain, head is last) |\n78|| 13.14.1 message-like inline content at most 64 KiB; oversized becomes a blob reference | `contentBlockForText`, `installOverflow` | `TestNormalizeInlineContentBoundary` (65536 inline, 65537 blob-referenced and byte-exact, never truncated) |\n79|| 13.14.1 same captured bytes project byte-identical output | `Normalize` (sorted inputs, no clock) | `TestNormalizeIsDeterministic` |\n80|| 13.14.1 unstable_archive cannot enter target projection | `Normalize` via `RefuseUnstableForTarget` | `TestNormalizeRefusesUnstableCapture` |\n81|| 13.14.1 capture closure: manifest link, blob fetch, digest/size agreement | `Normalize`, `collectMembers` | `TestNormalizeRefusalTable/manifest_closure_drift/tampered_blob/missing_blob` |\n82|| 13.14.1 framing-malformed records refuse with member+line named | `splitRecordLines`, `parseNativeLine`, body decoders | `TestNormalizeRefusalTable/malformed_json_line/missing_envelope_member/bad_envelope_version/blank_line/unknown_body_member/contradictory_protection/protected_plaintext_body/invalid_utf8_line` |\n83|| 13.14.1 live claims by captured history refuse | `deriveLiveSurface`, `resolveToolCalls` | `TestNormalizeRefusalTable/live_attestation_claim/live_followup_claim` |\n84|| 13.14.1 ambiguous tool pairings refuse | `resolveToolCalls` | `TestNormalizeRefusalTable/duplicate_call_id/duplicate_result_id` |\n85|| 13.14.1 exact actor mapping (referenced iff mapped) | `checkActors` | `TestNormalizeRefusalTable/unmapped_actor/unmapped_extra_actor/main_actor_in_map` |\n86|| 13.14.1 instruction authority and usage value model | `decodeInstructionBody`, `bodyUint53` | `TestNormalizeRefusalTable/bad_instruction_authority/fractional_usage/unsafe_usage_magnitude` |\n87|| 10.2 Blob Descriptor reference resolves to installed bytes | `installOverflow` | `TestNormalizeInlineContentBoundary` (`mustResolveOverflow` through the sink) |\n88|| 10.2 fsync + verify + atomic install before referencing | `InstallRawBlob`, `PutBlob` (landed) | `TestNormalizeIsIdempotentIntoSharedSink` (replay verifies and reuses, blob count stable) |\n89|| 7.8 large data by reference, never embedded | `contentBlockForText` | `TestNormalizeInlineContentBoundary` (65537-byte text is a reference, not an embedded frame) |\n90|| 1.6 string measure in characters | `environ.StringLength` at every native bound | `TestNormalizeRefusalTable` bound rows (call/actor/directive widths refuse past the character bound) |\n91|| 1.6 text is valid UTF-8, never rewritten | line-level `utf8.Valid` before decode | `TestNormalizeRefusalTable/invalid_utf8_line` |\n92|\n93|## Durability\n94|\n95|This package holds no local state. Its only durable write is\n96|overflow-blob installation: payload bytes through the landed\n97|`InstallRawBlob` (descriptor identity plus blob-ID/size agreement)\n98|and descriptor bytes through `ObjectStore.PutBlob`, both\n99|content-addressed under the landed no-replace discipline (stage,\n100|fsync, verify, atomic install). Crash semantics are the landed\n101|`localstore` discipline's (proven by that package's fault suites);\n102|this package adds bundle atomicity at the return:\n103|`TestNormalizeFailureReturnsNoPartialBundle` proves a mid-projection\n104|fetch failure returns no partial bundle and a healthy re-run\n105|converges, and `TestNormalizeIsIdempotentIntoSharedSink` proves a\n106|replay into a shared sink seals byte-identical output while the sink\n107|blob count stays stable (verify-and-reuse, no reinstall). A refused\n108|projection may leave orphan overflow blobs from earlier units in the\n109|sink; they are content-addressed and inert, and no bundle ever\n110|references them.\n111|\n112|## Mutants\n113|\n114|`testdata/mutant_harness.py` ships 49 narrowing rows plus the\n115|harmless `C-doc-comment` SURVIVED control. Every row weakens one\n116|gate to admit exactly one member of the class it must reject, and\n117|every killer drives the production `Normalize` entry over real\n118|captured bytes. `N-native-type-token` and `N-protection-encrypted`\n119|are the token-preserving attacks: the searched-for text still\n120|matches while the decision changes, and the killers execute the\n121|behavioral suite. No row is an arm-delete; no plant covers two\n122|sites. The battery runs twice with one raw log per plant per run\n123|carrying the subprocess exit.\n124|\n125|## Stated bounds (sibling scope, not waived)\n126|\n127|- The fixture-native record envelope is test-defined framing, not a\n128|  specification shape: `v`, `native_event_id`, `native_type`,\n129|  `origin`, `protection`, `actor`, `body`. Real providers define\n130|  their own native logs; the adapter layer is `sessadapter` scope.\n131|- Per-kind payload facts cover exactly the registry above. Other\n132|  Canonical kinds (`session_started`, `approval_request`,\n133|  `plan_update`, `progress`, `rate_limit`, `file_change`,\n134|  `compaction`, `turn_*`, `subagent_*`, `error`,\n135|  `migration_checkpoint`, `session_finished`) are never emitted\n136|  here; their fact registries are normalization-sibling scope.\n137|- Framing-malformed lines refuse (unparseable JSON, missing\n138|  envelope members, blank lines, invalid UTF-8, contradictory\n139|  protection claims, unknown body members inside a known type)\n140|  instead of projecting: without attributable identity a line\n141|  cannot become evidence. Type-level unknowns become\n142|  `opaque_event`.\n143|- Native-protected records carry no reason code: the closed core\n144|  reasons name foreign causes only, and extension reasons are\n145|  operator scope. The payload `protection` fact carries the cause.\n146|- Turn IDs and source timestamps are always null: turns are not\n147|  reconstructed and source clocks are not trusted.\n148|- Tool call arguments are not carried: calls are inert history\n149|  identified by call ID and tool name.\n150|- Unknown-class excluded members project nothing: their bytes were\n151|  never captured.\n152|- Sections 13.14.2-13.14.5 (fidelity dispositions, projection\n153|  planning, Migration Checkpoint, lineage, transaction, tuple\n154|  admission) are sibling scope: this story plans no projection,\n155|  stages no target, and admits no tuple.\n156|- Section 7.8 operation wiring (capture-plan/capture/normalize\n157|  frames) stays owned by `sessadapter`; this package owns the\n158|  fidelity rules those operations must satisfy, not the frames.\n159|- The `pending` live-work-order map parameter of\n160|  `deriveLiveSurface` is live-sibling API: `Normalize` always\n161|  passes nil, so nothing captured can pend.\n162|\n163|## Story-close (FINAL leaf)\n164|\n165|This leaf binds the story's normative sections in\n166|`internal/traceability/ownership.v0.7.0.json`:\n167|\n168|- `section:7.8` is bound FULL (2/2): clause `7.8#1` (large data by\n169|  reference) discharges through the new `clone-projection-fidelity`\n170|  acceptance case (`TestNormalizeInlineContentBoundary`); clause\n171|  `7.8#2` (execution bindings equal freshly read facts) discharges\n172|  through the new `session-adapter-call-binding` case\n173|  (`TestCheckCallBinding` plus the zero-facts refusal test, both\n174|  committed by the sessadapter owner).\n175|- `section:10.2` is bound FULL (5/5): `10.2#1` through\n176|  `clone-capture-contracts`, `10.2#3`–`10.2#5` through\n177|  `clone-native-capture`, and `10.2#2` through both\n178|  `clone-native-capture` (capture install) and\n179|  `clone-projection-fidelity` (overflow install and idempotent\n180|  replay).\n181|- `section:13.14.1` carries no RFC 2119 keyword line the\n182|  `tracecheck` scanner can see (its obligations are closed-shape\n183|  \"contains exactly\" sentences), so no registry binding can\n184|  enumerate it: it would measure `unmeasured`, which assigned-scope\n185|  admission deliberately refuses. The story's 13.14.1 clause record\n186|  is therefore the three package `TRACEABILITY.md` files plus the\n187|  three leaf conformance matrices, executed by the three real\n188|  suites bound as `clone-capture-contracts`, `clone-native-capture`,\n189|  and `clone-projection-fidelity`.\n190|- `reviewedOwnershipCanonicalSHA256` in\n191|  `internal/traceability/traceability.go` is re-derived from the\n192|  edited registry (derivation command and output in\n193|  `TASK-260830-32ypr2_results.md`).","final_result":true}}}
{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c67d","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0b3c6-628c-70a3-ad39-75274b1adfea"},"sequence":409,"recorded_at":1780531400000813,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"94f324ce-ad7a-4eb7-9c54-86bfc93d2b24","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.completed","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"94f324ce-ad7a-4eb7-9c54-86bfc93d2b24","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"94f324ce-ad7a-4eb7-9c54-86bfc93d2b24"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0b3c7-6705-76e2-af36-a2fa7c945823"},"task_id":"01a0b3c7-6705-76e2-af36-a2fa7c945823","event":{"kind":"completed","task_id":"01a0b3c7-6705-76e2-af36-a2fa7c945823"}}}
{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c67f","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0b3c6-628c-70a3-ad39-75274b1adfea"},"sequence":410,"recorded_at":1780531400000815,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"94f324ce-ad7a-4eb7-9c54-86bfc93d2b24","payload_type":"tool.result","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"tool_result","command_id":"94f324ce-ad7a-4eb7-9c54-86bfc93d2b24","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"94f324ce-ad7a-4eb7-9c54-86bfc93d2b24"},"call_id":"call_01a0b3c75fa7742d9f71eed30e900c87","text":"Read text file `internal/cloneproject/tools.go`.\n1|package cloneproject\n2|\n3|// This file folds historical tools: call/result pairing, the\n4|// completed/aborted resolution, the live surface that stays empty,\n5|// the effective instruction snapshot that excludes foreign history,\n6|// and the usage ledger that never becomes target accounting.\n7|\n8|import (\n9|\t\"sort\"\n10|)\n11|\n12|// Tool resolution statuses. Capture yields completed or aborted\n13|// only: a call resolves completed with exactly one tool_result and\n14|// becomes aborted history otherwise. Nothing captured is pending.\n15|const (\n16|\t// StatusCompleted marks a call paired with its result.\n17|\tStatusCompleted = \"completed\"\n18|\t// StatusAborted marks a call without its result, or a result\n19|\t// without its call: inert history with reason\n20|\t// unsafe_pending_action.\n21|\tStatusAborted = \"aborted\"\n22|)\n23|\n24|// ToolResolution is one folded tool call or orphan result.\n25|type ToolResolution struct {\n26|\t// CallID is the native call identifier.\n27|\tCallID string\n28|\t// ToolName is empty for orphan results, which name no call.\n29|\tToolName string\n30|\t// Status is completed or aborted.\n31|\tStatus string\n32|\t// ResultStatus is the paired result status (ok|error), empty\n33|\t// for calls without a result.\n34|\tResultStatus string\n35|}\n36|\n37|// toolCall is one observed tool/call record.\n38|type toolCall struct {\n39|\trecord NativeRecord\n40|\tbody   toolCallBody\n41|}\n42|\n43|// toolResult is one observed tool/result record.\n44|type toolResult struct {\n45|\trecord NativeRecord\n46|\tbody   toolResultBody\n47|}\n48|\n49|// resolveToolCalls pairs calls with results in record order. Two\n50|// calls sharing one ID refuse, two results sharing one ID refuse,\n51|// and a result claiming live followup refuses: captured history can\n52|// neither fork nor request a live action.\n53|func resolveToolCalls(calls []toolCall, results []toolResult) ([]ToolResolution, error) {\n54|\tseenCalls := map[string]toolCall{}\n55|\tfor _, call := range calls {\n56|\t\tif _, duplicate := seenCalls[call.body.CallID]; duplicate {\n57|\t\t\treturn nil, invalid(\"tool call %q is not unique\", call.body.CallID)\n58|\t\t}\n59|\t\tseenCalls[call.body.CallID] = call\n60|\t}\n61|\tseenResults := map[string]toolResult{}\n62|\tfor _, result := range results {\n63|\t\tif _, duplicate := seenResults[result.body.CallID]; duplicate {\n64|\t\t\treturn nil, invalid(\"tool result %q is not unique\", result.body.CallID)\n65|\t\t}\n66|\t\tseenResults[result.body.CallID] = result\n67|\t}\n68|\tfor _, result := range results {\n69|\t\tif result.body.LiveFollowup {\n70|\t\t\twhere := \"record \" + result.record.MemberKey + \" line \" + itoa(result.record.Line)\n71|\t\t\treturn nil, invalid(\"%s claims a live followup for historical tool result %q\", where, result.body.CallID)\n72|\t\t}\n73|\t}\n74|\tresolutions := make([]ToolResolution, 0, len(calls)+len(results))\n75|\tfor _, call := range calls {\n76|\t\tresult, ok := seenResults[call.body.CallID]\n77|\t\tif !ok {\n78|\t\t\tresolutions = append(resolutions, ToolResolution{\n79|\t\t\t\tCallID:   call.body.CallID,\n80|\t\t\t\tToolName: call.body.ToolName,\n81|\t\t\t\tStatus:   StatusAborted,\n82|\t\t\t})\n83|\t\t\tcontinue\n84|\t\t}\n85|\t\tresolutions = append(resolutions, ToolResolution{\n86|\t\t\tCallID:       call.body.CallID,\n87|\t\t\tToolName:     call.body.ToolName,\n88|\t\t\tStatus:       StatusCompleted,\n89|\t\t\tResultStatus: result.body.Status,\n90|\t\t})\n91|\t}\n92|\tfor _, result := range results {\n93|\t\tif _, ok := seenCalls[result.body.CallID]; !ok {\n94|\t\t\tresolutions = append(resolutions, ToolResolution{\n95|\t\t\t\tCallID:       result.body.CallID,\n96|\t\t\t\tStatus:       StatusAborted,\n97|\t\t\t\tResultStatus: result.body.Status,\n98|\t\t\t})\n99|\t\t}\n100|\t}\n101|\treturn resolutions, nil\n102|}\n103|\n104|// LiveSurface is the projection's live action surface: callable\n105|// tools and pending actions. Capture carries no live work order, so\n106|// both lists are always empty: historical tools are inert.\n107|type LiveSurface struct {\n108|\t// CallableTools names tools the target may call. Always empty\n109|\t// from captured history.\n110|\tCallableTools []string\n111|\t// PendingActions names call IDs awaiting execution. Always\n112|\t// empty from captured history.\n113|\tPendingActions []string\n114|}\n115|\n116|// toolDefinition is one observed tool/definition record.\n117|type toolDefinition struct {\n118|\trecord NativeRecord\n119|\tbody   toolDefinitionBody\n120|}\n121|\n122|// deriveLiveSurface folds historical definitions and resolutions.\n123|// A captured definition claiming live authority refuses instead of\n124|// registering: history can never self-promote to a callable tool.\n125|// Pending actions admit only completed calls named by a live work\n126|// order; aborted history never pends even when named.\n127|func deriveLiveSurface(definitions []toolDefinition, resolutions []ToolResolution, liveWorkOrders map[string]bool) (LiveSurface, error) {\n128|\tsurface := LiveSurface{}\n129|\tfor _, definition := range definitions {\n130|\t\tif definition.body.LiveClaim {\n131|\t\t\twhere := \"record \" + definition.record.MemberKey + \" line \" + itoa(definition.record.Line)\n132|\t\t\treturn LiveSurface{}, invalid(\"%s claims live authority for historical tool definition %q\", where, definition.body.ToolName)\n133|\t\t}\n134|\t}\n135|\tfor _, resolution := range resolutions {\n136|\t\tif resolution.Status == StatusAborted {\n137|\t\t\tcontinue\n138|\t\t}\n139|\t\tif liveWorkOrders[resolution.CallID] {\n140|\t\t\tsurface.PendingActions = append(surface.PendingActions, resolution.CallID)\n141|\t\t}\n142|\t}\n143|\tsort.Strings(surface.PendingActions)\n144|\treturn surface, nil\n145|}\n146|\n147|// EffectiveInstruction is the projected session's instruction\n148|// snapshot: the last native instruction in record order. Foreign\n149|// instructions are low-authority history and never change it.\n150|type EffectiveInstruction struct {\n151|\t// Found reports whether any native instruction was observed.\n152|\tFound bool\n153|\t// Authority is the native claimed authority, high or low.\n154|\tAuthority string\n155|\t// Directives are the native directives in record order.\n156|\tDirectives []string\n157|}\n158|\n159|// instructionObservation is one observed instruction/snapshot record.\n160|type instructionObservation struct {\n161|\trecord NativeRecord\n162|\tbody   instructionBody\n163|}\n164|\n165|// foldInstructions folds native instructions in record order. The\n166|// last native record wins; foreign records are history only and\n167|// never reach the snapshot.\n168|func foldInstructions(observations []instructionObservation) EffectiveInstruction {\n169|\teffective := EffectiveInstruction{}\n170|\tfor _, observation := range observations {\n171|\t\tif observation.record.Origin != \"native\" {\n172|\t\t\tcontinue\n173|\t\t}\n174|\t\teffective = EffectiveInstruction{\n175|\t\t\tFound:      true,\n176|\t\t\tAuthority:  observation.body.Authority,\n177|\t\t\tDirectives: append([]string(nil), observation.body.Directives...),\n178|\t\t}\n179|\t}\n180|\treturn effective\n181|}\n182|\n183|// UsageLedger separates source usage from target accounting. Source\n184|// records count into the source totals only; the target totals stay\n185|// zero: source usage is not target accounting.\n186|type UsageLedger struct {\n187|\tSourceInputTokens  uint64\n188|\tSourceOutputTokens uint64\n189|\tTargetInputTokens  uint64\n190|\tTargetOutputTokens uint64\n191|}\n192|\n193|// usageObservation is one observed usage/report record.\n194|type usageObservation struct {\n195|\trecord NativeRecord\n196|\tbody   usageBody\n197|}\n198|\n199|// foldUsage sums source tokens with overflow refusal. The target\n200|// totals are never written: no source record can fund them.\n201|func foldUsage(observations []usageObservation) (UsageLedger, error) {\n202|\tledger := UsageLedger{}\n203|\tfor _, observation := range observations {\n204|\t\tinput := ledger.SourceInputTokens + observation.body.InputTokens\n205|\t\tif input < ledger.SourceInputTokens || input > maxUint53 {\n206|\t\t\treturn UsageLedger{}, invalid(\"source input token total exceeds uint53\")\n207|\t\t}\n208|\t\toutput := ledger.SourceOutputTokens + observation.body.OutputTokens\n209|\t\tif output < ledger.SourceOutputTokens || output > maxUint53 {\n210|\t\t\treturn UsageLedger{}, invalid(\"source output token total exceeds uint53\")\n211|\t\t}\n212|\t\tledger.SourceInputTokens = input\n213|\t\tledger.SourceOutputTokens = output\n214|\t}\n215|\treturn ledger, nil\n216|}","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"read_file","outcome":"success"}}}
{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c681","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0b3c6-628c-70a3-ad39-75274b1adfea"},"sequence":411,"recorded_at":1780531400000817,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"94f324ce-ad7a-4eb7-9c54-86bfc93d2b24","payload_type":"tool.result","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"tool_result","command_id":"94f324ce-ad7a-4eb7-9c54-86bfc93d2b24","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"94f324ce-ad7a-4eb7-9c54-86bfc93d2b24"},"call_id":"call_01a0b3c7613877bfb6e97070b6008dcc","text":"Read text file `internal/cloneproject/TRACEABILITY.md`.\n1|# Projection Fidelity Clause Coverage (TASK-260830-32ypr2)\n2|\n3|Owner: `internal/cloneproject`. Authority:\n4|`internal/specdoc/SPEC.v0.7.0.md`, Sections 7.8, 10.2, 13.14.1\n5|(the pinned sections are byte-identical to v0.6.0).\n6|This is the FINAL leaf's clause record for the projection-fidelity\n7|closure; the `internal/traceability` registry bindings and re-pin\n8|ship in this leaf as well (see the Story-close section below).\n9|\n10|## Why this package normalizes instead of clonebundle or clonesnap\n11|\n12|The first leaf (`internal/clonebundle`) owns the capture contracts:\n13|the closed manifest/boundary/session/event shapes, their builders\n14|and decoders. The second leaf (`internal/clonesnap`) owns the\n15|capture OPERATION over a real provider store. This package owns\n16|NORMALIZATION: deriving Canonical Sessions and Canonical Events\n17|from captured bytes. Every event and the session seal through the\n18|landed `clonebundle` builders (`BuildCanonicalEvent`,\n19|`BuildCanonicalSession`, `CheckOrdinalContiguity`,\n20|`RefuseUnstableForTarget`, `InstallRawBlob`) and re-decode through\n21|the landed decoders before return; overflow Blob Descriptors seal\n22|through `clonesnap.BuildBlobDescriptor`; no second manifest,\n23|session, event, blob, or identity model exists here.\n24|\n25|## Landed-owner reuse\n26|\n27|| Scope | Owner | Use |\n28||---|---|---|\n29|| Session/event/evidence shapes | `internal/clonebundle` | all Build/Decode/Check/Refuse entries above |\n30|| Overflow descriptor shape | `internal/clonesnap` | `BuildBlobDescriptor` (errors wrapped with the overflow cause) |\n31|| Blob install (no-replace, fsync, verify) | `internal/clonebundle` + `internal/localstore` | `InstallRawBlob`, `ObjectStore.PutBlob` |\n32|| Digests, UUIDv7, timestamps | `internal/scalar` | `ParseDigest`, `SHA256Digest`, `ParseUUIDv7` |\n33|| Character string measure | `internal/environ` | `StringLength` at every native bound |\n34|| Canonical bytes | `internal/canonicaljson` | `Canonicalize`, `CalculateObjectIdentity` (tests resolve overflow descriptors) |\n35|\n36|## Fixture-native per-kind payload fact registry\n37|\n38|Section 13.14.1 requires payloads to carry only their registered\n39|typed facts. The envelope and value model are landed (`checkPayload`\n40|in `clonebundle`); this package registers the exact facts it emits\n41|for each kind it projects. No other Canonical kind is emitted here.\n42|\n43|| Kind | Exact facts |\n44||---|---|\n45|| `user_message`, `assistant_message`, `reasoning_summary` | `content_blocks` (one `text` block, inline at or under 64 KiB, else `blob_descriptor_id` + `media_type`), `extensions` |\n46|| `opaque_reasoning` | `protection` (`encrypted`\\|`signed`), `byte_count`, `blob_descriptor_id`, `extensions` |\n47|| `opaque_event` (unknown record) | `native_type`, `byte_count`, `blob_descriptor_id`, `extensions` |\n48|| `opaque_event` (protected known record) | `native_type`, `protection`, `byte_count`, `blob_descriptor_id`, `extensions` |\n49|| `opaque_event` (unknown member) | `native_item_key`, `byte_count`, `blob_descriptor_id`, `extensions` |\n50|| `instruction_snapshot` | `authority` (`low` forced for foreign), `directives`, `extensions` |\n51|| `tool_definition_snapshot` | `tool_name`, `definition_digest`, `callable` (always false), `extensions` |\n52|| `tool_call` | `call_id`, `tool_name`, `resolution` (`completed`\\|`aborted`), `extensions` |\n53|| `tool_result` | `call_id`, `status` (`ok`\\|`error`), `resolution`, `extensions` |\n54|| `usage` | `input_tokens`, `output_tokens`, `extensions` |\n55|\n56|## Clause map\n57|\n58|| Pinned clause | Production entry | Test |\n59||---|---|---|\n60|| 13.14.1 unknown native records become raw-addressable opaque events | `Normalize`, `dispatchRecord` | `TestNormalizeUnknownRecordBecomesOpaqueEvent` (kind, `opaque` visibility, `unknown_native_event` reason, raw range resolves to the exact line) |\n61|| 13.14.1 almost-known records are never coerced into a neighbouring kind | `dispatchRecord` (exact type switch) | `TestNormalizeAlmostKnownRecordBecomesOpaqueEvent` (`message/smoke` stays `opaque_event`, never `user_message`) |\n62|| 13.14.1 unknown-class members become whole-member opaque events | `collectMembers` | `TestNormalizeUnknownMemberBecomesWholeMemberOpaque` (offset 0, full length, null native IDs, resolves to the whole member) |\n63|| 13.14.1 opaque events are never dropped, guessed, or re-typed | `Normalize` (deterministic order) | `TestNormalizeOpaqueIsStableAcrossProjections` (project twice, byte-identical, still `opaque_event`) |\n64|| 13.14.1 foreign encrypted reasoning is opaque-preserved | `dispatchProtected` | `TestNormalizeForeignEncryptedReasoningStaysOpaque` (`opaque_reasoning`, `foreign_encrypted_payload`, no content members, byte-exact round trip) |\n65|| 13.14.1 foreign signed reasoning is opaque-preserved | `dispatchProtected` | `TestNormalizeForeignSignedReasoningStaysOpaque` (`foreign_signature_unverifiable`, byte-exact) |\n66|| 13.14.1 native protected reasoning stays opaque with no foreign code | `dispatchProtected`, `cryptoReasons` | `TestNormalizeNativeProtectedReasoningStaysOpaque` (empty reasons) |\n67|| 13.14.1 protected known content never reaches a semantic kind | `dispatchProtected` | `TestNormalizeProtectedMessageBecomesOpaqueEvent` (encrypted assistant message is `opaque_event`) |\n68|| 13.14.1 unknown+protected records carry both stable reasons | `dispatchProtected` | `TestNormalizeUnknownProtectedRecordCarriesBothReasons` |\n69|| 13.14.1 foreign instructions are low-authority history | `dispatchInstruction`, `foldInstructions` | `TestNormalizeForeignInstructionCannotChangeEffectiveSnapshot` (effective snapshot native-only, foreign payload pins `low`), `TestNormalizeForeignOnlyInstructionLeavesSnapshotEmpty` |\n70|| 13.14.1 source usage is not target accounting | `foldUsage` | `TestNormalizeSourceUsageIsNotTargetAccounting` (source sums exact, target zero) |\n71|| 13.14.1 historical tools are inert; call+result resolves completed | `resolveToolCalls`, `deriveLiveSurface` | `TestNormalizeToolMatrix/call_with_result` (kinds, `internal` visibility, `completed`, empty live surface) |\n72|| 13.14.1 incomplete calls become aborted history and block pending action | `resolveToolCalls`, `deriveLiveSurface` | `TestNormalizeToolMatrix/call_without_result` (`aborted`, `unsafe_pending_action`, empty live surface), `TestNormalizeToolMatrix/result_without_call` (orphan `aborted`) |\n73|| 13.14.1 results arriving after the boundary complete the same call | `resolveToolCalls` over two captures | `TestNormalizeResultAfterBoundaryCompletes` (first capture `aborted`, second `completed`) |\n74|| 13.14.1 nested calls attribute to a parented subagent actor | `checkActors`, `buildResult` | `TestNormalizeToolMatrix/nested_subagent_call` (subagent actor, parent is main) |\n75|| 13.14.1 definitions never register a callable tool | `deriveLiveSurface`, `dispatchDefinition` | `TestNormalizeToolDefinitionNeverRegistersCallable` (`callable` false, `CallableTools` empty) |\n76|| 13.14.1 live surface stays empty over mixed history | `deriveLiveSurface` | `TestNormalizeLiveSurfaceStaysEmpty` |\n77|| 13.14.1 Canonical Session bounds (actors, ordered event IDs, head) | `buildResult` | `TestNormalizeSealsSessionShape` (ordinals, parent chain, head is last) |\n78|| 13.14.1 message-like inline content at most 64 KiB; oversized becomes a blob reference | `contentBlockForText`, `installOverflow` | `TestNormalizeInlineContentBoundary` (65536 inline, 65537 blob-referenced and byte-exact, never truncated) |\n79|| 13.14.1 same captured bytes project byte-identical output | `Normalize` (sorted inputs, no clock) | `TestNormalizeIsDeterministic` |\n80|| 13.14.1 unstable_archive cannot enter target projection | `Normalize` via `RefuseUnstableForTarget` | `TestNormalizeRefusesUnstableCapture` |\n81|| 13.14.1 capture closure: manifest link, blob fetch, digest/size agreement | `Normalize`, `collectMembers` | `TestNormalizeRefusalTable/manifest_closure_drift/tampered_blob/missing_blob` |\n82|| 13.14.1 framing-malformed records refuse with member+line named | `splitRecordLines`, `parseNativeLine`, body decoders | `TestNormalizeRefusalTable/malformed_json_line/missing_envelope_member/bad_envelope_version/blank_line/unknown_body_member/contradictory_protection/protected_plaintext_body/invalid_utf8_line` |\n83|| 13.14.1 live claims by captured history refuse | `deriveLiveSurface`, `resolveToolCalls` | `TestNormalizeRefusalTable/live_attestation_claim/live_followup_claim` |\n84|| 13.14.1 ambiguous tool pairings refuse | `resolveToolCalls` | `TestNormalizeRefusalTable/duplicate_call_id/duplicate_result_id` |\n85|| 13.14.1 exact actor mapping (referenced iff mapped) | `checkActors` | `TestNormalizeRefusalTable/unmapped_actor/unmapped_extra_actor/main_actor_in_map` |\n86|| 13.14.1 instruction authority and usage value model | `decodeInstructionBody`, `bodyUint53` | `TestNormalizeRefusalTable/bad_instruction_authority/fractional_usage/unsafe_usage_magnitude` |\n87|| 10.2 Blob Descriptor reference resolves to installed bytes | `installOverflow` | `TestNormalizeInlineContentBoundary` (`mustResolveOverflow` through the sink) |\n88|| 10.2 fsync + verify + atomic install before referencing | `InstallRawBlob`, `PutBlob` (landed) | `TestNormalizeIsIdempotentIntoSharedSink` (replay verifies and reuses, blob count stable) |\n89|| 7.8 large data by reference, never embedded | `contentBlockForText` | `TestNormalizeInlineContentBoundary` (65537-byte text is a reference, not an embedded frame) |\n90|| 1.6 string measure in characters | `environ.StringLength` at every native bound | `TestNormalizeRefusalTable` bound rows (call/actor/directive widths refuse past the character bound) |\n91|| 1.6 text is valid UTF-8, never rewritten | line-level `utf8.Valid` before decode | `TestNormalizeRefusalTable/invalid_utf8_line` |\n92|\n93|## Durability\n94|\n95|This package holds no local state. Its only durable write is\n96|overflow-blob installation: payload bytes through the landed\n97|`InstallRawBlob` (descriptor identity plus blob-ID/size agreement)\n98|and descriptor bytes through `ObjectStore.PutBlob`, both\n99|content-addressed under the landed no-replace discipline (stage,\n100|fsync, verify, atomic install). Crash semantics are the landed\n101|`localstore` discipline's (proven by that package's fault suites);\n102|this package adds bundle atomicity at the return:\n103|`TestNormalizeFailureReturnsNoPartialBundle` proves a mid-projection\n104|fetch failure returns no partial bundle and a healthy re-run\n105|converges, and `TestNormalizeIsIdempotentIntoSharedSink` proves a\n106|replay into a shared sink seals byte-identical output while the sink\n107|blob count stays stable (verify-and-reuse, no reinstall). A refused\n108|projection may leave orphan overflow blobs from earlier units in the\n109|sink; they are content-addressed and inert, and no bundle ever\n110|references them.\n111|\n112|## Mutants\n113|\n114|`testdata/mutant_harness.py` ships 49 narrowing rows plus the\n115|harmless `C-doc-comment` SURVIVED control. Every row weakens one\n116|gate to admit exactly one member of the class it must reject, and\n117|every killer drives the production `Normalize` entry over real\n118|captured bytes. `N-native-type-token` and `N-protection-encrypted`\n119|are the token-preserving attacks: the searched-for text still\n120|matches while the decision changes, and the killers execute the\n121|behavioral suite. No row is an arm-delete; no plant covers two\n122|sites. The battery runs twice with one raw log per plant per run\n123|carrying the subprocess exit.\n124|\n125|## Stated bounds (sibling scope, not waived)\n126|\n127|- The fixture-native record envelope is test-defined framing, not a\n128|  specification shape: `v`, `native_event_id`, `native_type`,\n129|  `origin`, `protection`, `actor`, `body`. Real providers define\n130|  their own native logs; the adapter layer is `sessadapter` scope.\n131|- Per-kind payload facts cover exactly the registry above. Other\n132|  Canonical kinds (`session_started`, `approval_request`,\n133|  `plan_update`, `progress`, `rate_limit`, `file_change`,\n134|  `compaction`, `turn_*`, `subagent_*`, `error`,\n135|  `migration_checkpoint`, `session_finished`) are never emitted\n136|  here; their fact registries are normalization-sibling scope.\n137|- Framing-malformed lines refuse (unparseable JSON, missing\n138|  envelope members, blank lines, invalid UTF-8, contradictory\n139|  protection claims, unknown body members inside a known type)\n140|  instead of projecting: without attributable identity a line\n141|  cannot become evidence. Type-level unknowns become\n142|  `opaque_event`.\n143|- Native-protected records carry no reason code: the closed core\n144|  reasons name foreign causes only, and extension reasons are\n145|  operator scope. The payload `protection` fact carries the cause.\n146|- Turn IDs and source timestamps are always null: turns are not\n147|  reconstructed and source clocks are not trusted.\n148|- Tool call arguments are not carried: calls are inert history\n149|  identified by call ID and tool name.\n150|- Unknown-class excluded members project nothing: their bytes were\n151|  never captured.\n152|- Sections 13.14.2-13.14.5 (fidelity dispositions, projection\n153|  planning, Migration Checkpoint, lineage, transaction, tuple\n154|  admission) are sibling scope: this story plans no projection,\n155|  stages no target, and admits no tuple.\n156|- Section 7.8 operation wiring (capture-plan/capture/normalize\n157|  frames) stays owned by `sessadapter`; this package owns the\n158|  fidelity rules those operations must satisfy, not the frames.\n159|- The `pending` live-work-order map parameter of\n160|  `deriveLiveSurface` is live-sibling API: `Normalize` always\n161|  passes nil, so nothing captured can pend.\n162|\n163|## Story-close (FINAL leaf)\n164|\n165|This leaf binds the story's normative sections in\n166|`internal/traceability/ownership.v0.7.0.json`:\n167|\n168|- `section:7.8` is bound FULL (2/2): clause `7.8#1` (large data by\n169|  reference) discharges through the new `clone-projection-fidelity`\n170|  acceptance case (`TestNormalizeInlineContentBoundary`); clause\n171|  `7.8#2` (execution bindings equal freshly read facts) discharges\n172|  through the new `session-adapter-call-binding` case\n173|  (`TestCheckCallBinding` plus the zero-facts refusal test, both\n174|  committed by the sessadapter owner).\n175|- `section:10.2` is bound FULL (5/5): `10.2#1` through\n176|  `clone-capture-contracts`, `10.2#3`–`10.2#5` through\n177|  `clone-native-capture`, and `10.2#2` through both\n178|  `clone-native-capture` (capture install) and\n179|  `clone-projection-fidelity` (overflow install and idempotent\n180|  replay).\n181|- `section:13.14.1` carries no RFC 2119 keyword line the\n182|  `tracecheck` scanner can see (its obligations are closed-shape\n183|  \"contains exactly\" sentences), so no registry binding can\n184|  enumerate it: it would measure `unmeasured`, which assigned-scope\n185|  admission deliberately refuses. The story's 13.14.1 clause record\n186|  is therefore the three package `TRACEABILITY.md` files plus the\n187|  three leaf conformance matrices, executed by the three real\n188|  suites bound as `clone-capture-contracts`, `clone-native-capture`,\n189|  and `clone-projection-fidelity`.\n190|- `reviewedOwnershipCanonicalSHA256` in\n191|  `internal/traceability/traceability.go` is re-derived from the\n192|  edited registry (derivation command and output in\n193|  `TASK-260830-32ypr2_results.md`).","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"read_file","outcome":"success"}}}
{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c683","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0b3c6-628c-70a3-ad39-75274b1adfea"},"sequence":412,"recorded_at":1780531400000819,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"94f324ce-ad7a-4eb7-9c54-86bfc93d2b24","payload_type":"tool.result","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"tool_result","command_id":"94f324ce-ad7a-4eb7-9c54-86bfc93d2b24","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"94f324ce-ad7a-4eb7-9c54-86bfc93d2b24"},"call_id":"call_01a0b3c762b67009ae8eb0844b036450","text":"Read text file `internal/cloneproject/doc.go`.\n1|package cloneproject\n2|\n3|// This package implements the Section 13.14.1 projection-fidelity\n4|// closure: Normalize derives a Canonical Session and Canonical Events\n5|// from captured bytes (a sealed Clone Capture Manifest, its sealed\n6|// Clone Raw Object Manifest, and the installed payload blobs). It is\n7|// the final leaf of the canonical-session-capture-and-evidence\n8|// story: contracts come from internal/clonebundle, capture from\n9|// internal/clonesnap, and this package owns normalization only.\n10|//\n11|// Authority: relux-works/agent-session-manager-spec@v0.7.0, Sections\n12|// 7.8, 10.2, and 13.14.1 (internal/specdoc/SPEC.v0.7.0.md).\n13|//\n14|// The projection input is captured bytes, never hand-written\n15|// Canonical Events: every proof builds a fixture provider store,\n16|// runs clonesnap.Capture over it, and normalizes the sealed output.\n17|// Identical captured bytes produce byte-identical canonical output.\n18|//\n19|// Native records: the provider-native session log this package reads\n20|// is newline-delimited JSON (one record per line) carried by included\n21|// durable capture members. The envelope is fixture-native and NOT a\n22|// specification shape:\n23|//\n24|//\t{\"v\":1,\"native_event_id\":\"...\",\"native_type\":\"...\",\n25|//\t \"origin\":\"native|foreign\",\"protection\":\"none|encrypted|signed\",\n26|//\t \"actor\":\"main|subagent:<name>|external\",\"body\":{...}}\n27|//\n28|// Projection rules (each driven and mutated, see TRACEABILITY.md):\n29|//\n30|//   - Unknown native types become raw-addressable opaque_event\n31|//     records with opaque visibility, a whole-record byte-range\n32|//     reference, and reason unknown_native_event. Unknown-class\n33|//     members become one whole-member opaque_event. Nothing\n34|//     attributable is dropped, guessed, or re-typed.\n35|//   - Foreign encrypted/signed reasoning becomes opaque_reasoning\n36|//     with opaque visibility, preserved byte-exact through the blob\n37|//     store, never decrypted, re-encoded, summarized, truncated, or\n38|//     promoted. Foreign instructions are low-authority history: they\n39|//     never change the effective instruction snapshot.\n40|//   - Historical tools are inert. A tool_definition_snapshot never\n41|//     registers a callable tool (a captured live claim refuses).\n42|//     A tool_call resolves completed only with its tool_result;\n43|//     otherwise it becomes aborted history with reason\n44|//     unsafe_pending_action. Pending actions require a live work\n45|//     order, which capture never carries, so the live surface is\n46|//     always empty.\n47|//   - Source usage is counted into the source ledger only; target\n48|//     accounting stays zero.\n49|//   - Message-like text over 64 KiB becomes a Blob Descriptor\n50|//     reference to an installed overflow blob, never a truncation.\n51|//\n52|// Reuse, not fork: manifests, sessions, events, evidence, and the\n53|// unstable/maximal-safe gates come from internal/clonebundle;\n54|// overflow Blob Descriptors seal through clonesnap.BuildBlobDescriptor\n55|// and install through clonebundle.InstallRawBlob onto the landed\n56|// localstore no-replace discipline; digests, UUIDv7, and character\n57|// measures come from internal/scalar and internal/environ. No rule\n58|// is reimplemented where a landed owner exists.\n59|//\n60|// Stated bounds (not waived): the fixture-native record envelope is\n61|// test-defined, not a specification shape; per-kind payload fact\n62|// registries cover exactly the facts this package emits for the nine\n63|// fixture-native known types (other Canonical kinds are never\n64|// emitted here); framing-malformed lines (unparseable JSON, missing\n65|// envelope members, contradictory protection claims, unknown body\n66|// members) refuse instead of projecting; turn IDs and source\n67|// timestamps are always null; tool call arguments are not carried;\n68|// unknown-class excluded members project nothing (their bytes were\n69|// never captured); 13.14.2-13.14.5 (fidelity dispositions,\n70|// projection planning, transaction, lineage) are sibling scope.","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"read_file","outcome":"success"}}}
