{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c6c1","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0b3c6-628c-70a3-ad39-75274b1adfea"},"sequence":443,"recorded_at":1780531400000881,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"94f324ce-ad7a-4eb7-9c54-86bfc93d2b24","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"94f324ce-ad7a-4eb7-9c54-86bfc93d2b24","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"94f324ce-ad7a-4eb7-9c54-86bfc93d2b24"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0b3c7-774b-7ed2-a83a-c321a5b076c8"},"task_id":"01a0b3c7-774b-7ed2-a83a-c321a5b076c8","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a0b3c7-774b-7ed2-a83a-c321a5b076c8","chunk":"Read text file `internal/clonesnap/TRACEABILITY.md`.\n1|# Native Capture Clause Coverage (TASK-260830-2g5be6)\n2|\n3|Owner: `internal/clonesnap`. Authority:\n4|`internal/specdoc/SPEC.v0.7.0.md`, Sections 7.8, 10.2, 13.14.1\n5|(the pinned sections are byte-identical to v0.6.0).\n6|The Story's FINAL leaf carries the `internal/traceability` registry\n7|bindings and re-pin; this file is the second-leaf clause record.\n8|\n9|## Why this package captures instead of clonebundle\n10|\n11|The predecessor leaf (`internal/clonebundle`) owns the capture\n12|contracts: the closed manifest/boundary/blob/identity shapes, their\n13|builders and decoders. This package owns the capture OPERATION over\n14|a real on-disk provider store: the contained walk, item\n15|classification, boundary construction from measured evidence, the\n16|source-race check, the workspace checkpoint, and target admission.\n17|Every artifact emitted here is produced through the landed\n18|clonebundle builders (`BuildRawObjectManifest`,\n19|`BuildCaptureManifest`, `SanitizeNativeKey`, `CheckDigestsEqual`,\n20|`RefuseUnstableForTarget`, `RefuseMaximalSafeUnlessComplete`,\n21|`InstallRawBlob`, `VerifyDescriptorAgreement`,\n22|`DecodeWorkspaceBinding`, `IdentityDigest`) and re-decoded by the\n23|landed decoders before it is published or returned; no second\n24|manifest, boundary, blob, or identity model exists here.\n25|\n26|## Landed-owner reuse\n27|\n28|| Scope | Owner | Use |\n29||---|---|---|\n30|| Manifest/boundary/item/identity shapes | `internal/clonebundle` | all Build/Decode/Refuse entries above |\n31|| Store containment (openat-relative Guard walk) | `internal/secprim` | every payload open via `Guard.Open` from a verified root handle; member grammar via `CheckMemberPath` |\n32|| Durable writes (no-replace, fsync, verify) | `internal/localstore` | payload blobs via `InstallRawBlob`, manifests and receipts via `ObjectStore.PutBlob` |\n33|| Blob Descriptor shape and identity | `internal/canonicaljson` | `CalculateObjectIdentity` plus local claim comparisons; never the attesting entry |\n34|| Capture class vocabulary | `internal/clonebundle` | `ValidCaptureClass` (mirrors the `sessadapter` plan vocabulary) |\n35|| String measure, digests, UUIDv7, paths | `internal/environ`, `internal/scalar` | `StringLength`, `ParseDigest`, `ParseUUIDv7`, `ParseRelativePath`, `ParseAbsolutePath` |\n36|| Canonical bytes | `internal/canonicaljson` | `Canonicalize` for the workspace binding and the admission receipt |\n37|\n38|## Clause map\n39|\n40|| Pinned clause | Production entry | Test |\n41||---|---|---|\n42|| 13.14.1 Raw Manifest from real bytes: sorted unique entries, sanitized key, class, byte count, blob ID, descriptor ID | `Capture`, `BuildRawObjectManifest` (landed) | `TestCaptureSealsBothManifestsFromStoreBytes`, `TestCaptureIsByteIdenticalAcrossRuns` |\n43|| 13.14.1 Capture Manifest from real evidence: basis, boundary, items, excluded classes, derived raw_complete | `Capture`, `BuildCaptureManifest` (landed) | `TestCaptureSealsBothManifestsFromStoreBytes`, `TestCaptureOptionalAbsentSealsExcluded` |\n44|| 13.14.1 CaptureItem 9-class vocabulary + included/excluded content rule | `checkPlan` via `ValidCaptureClass`, `sealAndPublish` | `TestCaptureSealsBothManifestsFromStoreBytes`, `TestCaptureRefusesMysteryPlanClass` |\n45|| 13.14.1 always-excluded classes never included; bytes never reach blob/manifest/log/error | `excludedClass` (never opened) | `TestCaptureExcludesSecrets` (one fixture member per class, full-artifact scan) |\n46|| 13.14.1 unknown makes raw_complete false and blocks maximal_safe | `sealAndPublish`, `AdmitForTarget` via `RefuseMaximalSafeUnlessComplete` | `TestCaptureUnknownMakesRawIncomplete` (included), `TestCaptureOptionalAbsentUnknownMakesRawIncomplete` (excluded, P3-ε), `TestProjectMaximalSafeRequiresComplete`, `TestProjectMaximalSafeAdmitsComplete`, `TestProjectStrictExactAdmitsUnknown` |\n47|| 13.14.1 stable boundary: closed proof kind, generation, equal pre/post digests, idle facts | `sealAndPublish` via `buildBoundary` (landed) | `TestCaptureSealsBothManifestsFromStoreBytes`, `TestCaptureImmutableSnapshotProof` |\n48|| 13.14.1 size equality is never proof | `checkSourceRace` via `CheckDigestsEqual` | `TestCaptureRaceChangedByte` (equal-size differing bytes refuse) |\n49|| 13.14.1 unstable_archive: generation, pre/post, source_not_quiescent, explicit ack, target forbidden; core-created, archive-only | `raceOutcome`, `sealAndPublish` (`Core: true`) | `TestCaptureArchiveSealsUnstable` (literal kind/reason/ack/forbidden assertions + sealed pre/post digests equal the measured digests + sealed generation equals the request generation; `N-unstable-seals-pre-as-post` KILLED) |\n50|| 13.14.1 G2 rejects unstable | `AdmitForTarget` via `RefuseUnstableForTarget` | `TestProjectRefusesUnstable` (refusal + target sink empty), `TestProjectRefusesUnstableDirect` |\n51|| Source race detected before projection: changed byte/size, appended record, replaced file, unreadable at post, excluded size change | `walkAndMeasure`, `measurePost`, `gateSourceRace` | `TestCaptureRaceChangedByte/ChangedSize/AppendedRecord/ReplacedFile/RemovedFile/UnreadableAtPost/ExcludedSizeChange` (excluded row pins the \"size changes still race\" claim; `N-excluded-size` KILLED) |\n52|| Race gate precedes any seal or projection output | `Capture`, `CaptureAndProject` (ORDER-PIN) | `TestCaptureRaceSealsNoManifest` (no manifest published), `TestCaptureRaceEmitsNoReceipt` (race refusal, not a seal error, + target sink empty + capture store holds no sealed manifest; `N-race-order-project` killed by the seal error message, `N-race-order-project-seal` killed by the capture-store scan) |\n53|| 13.14.1 WorkspaceBinding from real state: normalized cwd, sorted unique fingerprints[0..128], branch, head/index/tree | `CheckpointWorkspace` via `DecodeWorkspaceBinding` (landed) | `TestCheckpointWorkspaceSealsObservedState`, `...RelativeCwd`, `...RootCwd`, refusal rows |\n54|| 13.14.1 no member grants filesystem authority | `workspaceCwdRelative` | `TestCheckpointWorkspaceRefusesEscape/DotSegments/MissingCwd/FileCwd/SymlinkRoot` |\n55|| 13.14.1 source basis ax_session / external_native | `Capture` via `buildSourceBasis` (landed) | `TestCaptureExternalNativeBasis`, `TestCaptureRefusesMixedSourceBasis/UnknownBasisKind/UnsanitizedExternalRef` |\n56|| SourceIdentity re-validated at the entry (P3-η, this leaf) | `Capture` via `IdentityDigest` (landed, re-decodes) | `TestCaptureRefusesInvalidSourceIdentity` (overlong ID, bogus kind, zero workspace, bad UTF-8, absolute ref; no manifest published) |\n57|| 10.2 fsync + verify + atomic install before publishing a referencing record | `InstallRawBlob`, `PutBlob` (landed) | `TestCaptureInstallsEveryPayloadBlob` (every entry's blob present), crash replay assertion, `TestCaptureSealsBothManifestsFromStoreBytes`, `TestProjectIsIdempotent` |\n58|| 10.2 logs record digest, size, media type only | `CaptureLog` (no byte parameter) | `TestCaptureLogRecordsDigestsOnly`, `TestCaptureExcludesSecrets` (log scan) |\n59|| 10.2 Blob Descriptor: sorted contiguous non-overlapping chunks from zero covering size; index from zero by one; empty = size zero, no chunks | `BuildBlobDescriptor` via `CalculateObjectIdentity` + `VerifyDescriptorAgreement` | `TestCaptureEmptyMemberSealsEmptyBlob`, `TestCaptureMultiChunkMember`, `TestCaptureDescriptorAgreementEndToEnd` |\n60|| 10.2 oversized blob fails with capability_unavailable before a partial manifest | `openMember` limit gate | `TestCaptureRefusesOversizedMember`, `TestCaptureRefusesSparseOversizedMember`, `TestDefaultMaxSingleBytesIs128GiB` |\n61|| 7.8 fidelity profiles strict_exact\\|maximal_safe\\|compact\\|messages_only | `AdmitForTarget`, `BuildAdmissionReceipt` | `TestProjectAdmitsStableEveryProfile`, `TestProjectRefusesUnknownProfile` |\n62|| 1.6 string measure in characters | measured gate: landed `DecodeWorkspaceBinding`; local `workspaceNullableText` via `environ.StringLength` is defence in depth | `TestCheckpointWorkspaceMultibyteBranch` (1024 two-byte characters seal, 1025 refuse with `string[1..1024]`; the `maximum+1` narrowing survives because the landed decoder refuses first — reviewer plant `R2-branch-1025` SURVIVED 2/2) |\n63|| Containment: symlinked intermediate and FIFO refuse before any payload open, member named; no escape past the root | `openMember` via `secprim.Guard`, store-root handle via `secprim.OpenNoFollowDir` | `TestCaptureRefusesSymlinkedIntermediate/OptionalSymlinkedIntermediate/TrailingSymlink/FIFO/OptionalFIFO/DirectoryMember/ParentPlanKey/SymlinkedStoreRoot` (`N-store-root-symlink`, `N-required-blocked-ancestor` KILLED) |\n64|| Plan member-name grammar: no escape past the root | `checkPlan` via `secprim.CheckMemberPath` (the only gate: `SanitizeNativeKey` admits parent segments) | `TestCaptureRefusesParentPlanKey` (`N-plan-grammar-dotdot` KILLED) |\n65|| Workspace fingerprints at most 128 | `workspaceFingerprints` | `TestCheckpointWorkspaceRefusesTooManyFingerprints` (killed by the local `maximum is 128` literal; `N-fingerprints-129` KILLED) |\n66|| First chunk of a multi-chunk blob within uint53[1..4194304] | `BuildBlobDescriptor` via `VerifyDescriptorAgreement` (landed) | `TestCaptureMultiChunkMember` (`N-first-chunk-oversize` KILLED) |\n67|| Unplanned members refuse; one item per plan candidate | `planMemberClass` | `TestCaptureRefusesUnplannedMember/PrefixSibling/RequiredMissing/DuplicatePlanKey/UnplannedSpecialMember` (unplanned symlink refuses `not a plan candidate` with no outside byte installed; `N-unplanned-special` KILLED) |\n68|\n69|## Durability\n70|\n71|This package performs durable writes only through\n72|`localstore.ObjectStore.PutBlob`: payload blobs (via the landed\n73|`InstallRawBlob`), manifest blobs, and admission receipt blobs. The\n74|landed discipline (stage, fsync, size/digest verification, atomic\n75|no-replace install, directory fsync, quarantine on mismatch) carries\n76|the crash semantics; this package adds the publish ORDER (payloads,\n77|then raw, then capture, then receipt) and the hooks that pin it.\n78|`TestCaptureCrashChildSelfTerminates` kills a live capture between\n79|the raw and capture publishes and proves the replay converges with\n80|byte-identical manifests; `TestProjectIsIdempotent` proves a\n81|replayed capture verifies and reuses every blob and publishes no\n82|half-written manifest (every manifest blob re-decodes). No second\n83|write path exists in this package.\n84|\n85|## Stated bounds (sibling scope, not waived)\n86|\n87|- No `ax` CLI, no provider process, no network: the store is a\n88|  fixture directory. Section 7.8 capture-plan/capture/normalize\n89|  operation wiring stays owned by `sessadapter`; this package\n90|  consumes plan keys and classes, it does not speak the adapter\n91|  protocol.\n92|- The sealed stable proof carries the two measured source digests\n93|  (pre and post): the race gate proved them equal before the seal\n94|  ran, so on the stable path the sealed bytes equal either\n95|  measurement, and the landed builder refuses unequal digests.\n96|  The ordering mutants move the gate after the seal:\n97|  `N-race-order-capture` is killed by the published manifests,\n98|  `N-race-order-project` by the seal error message (not by a sink\n99|  assertion), and `N-race-order-project-seal` — which preserves\n100|  the race error while sealing first — by the sealed raw manifest\n101|  in the capture store. Together they prove the gate precedes the\n102|  seal at both entries.\n103|- Excluded-class bytes are never opened, so a changed byte at\n104|  equal size inside an excluded member is below the detection\n105|  floor: presence, shape, and size changes still race, pinned by\n106|  `TestCaptureRaceExcludedSizeChange` (`N-excluded-size` KILLED).\n107|  Excluded bytes cannot affect capture output, and the never-open\n108|  rule is what the leak suite proves.\n109|- Enumeration observes names through path strings; every OPEN\n110|  descends from the verified root handle through the Guard. A\n111|  sub-walk transient swap restored before the post measurement is\n112|  below the detection floor (no filesystem snapshot); any\n113|  persistent change races, and blob integrity of the read bytes is\n114|  guaranteed by the install-time verification regardless.\n115|- Optional included-class candidates absent from the store seal as\n116|  excluded rows with reason `plan_optional_absent`; required ones\n117|  refuse. Required-ness for excluded classes is inert (presence is\n118|  irrelevant to bytes that are never opened).\n119|- `MaxSingleBytes` mirrors the Section 7.8 `ResourceLimits`\n120|  per-object bound; zero selects the Section 10.2 default of\n121|  137438953472 (32768 chunks of 4194304 bytes). The sparse\n122|  oversized row pins the default end to end without reading 128\n123|  GiB.\n124|- The admission receipt (`urn:ax:internal:clonesnap-admission-receipt`\n125|  1.0.0) proves target admission and race-before-projection\n126|  ordering only. Projection planning past admission, per-kind\n127|  event payload registries, and `strict_exact`/`compact`/\n128|  `messages_only` planning semantics are the final leaf's and the\n129|  normalization sibling's.\n130|- `internal/traceability` registry bindings and digest re-pin\n131|  (Story FINAL leaf).\n132|- The four-profile fidelity vocabulary is spelled twice:\n133|  `sessadapter` owns an unexported table and this package owns a\n134|  closed switch (P3-ζ′). The FINAL leaf unifies or exports one\n135|  owner; both spellings are pinned by their own suites today.\n136|- `EncodeNativeIdentity` standalone trusts the caller for bounds,\n137|  vocabulary, and the workspace ID (P3-η remainder): this leaf's\n138|  seal path re-decodes through the landed callers\n139|  (`sealAndPublish` calls `IdentityDigest` directly and\n140|  `BuildCaptureManifest` re-decodes the source identity\n141|  internally), pinned by `TestCaptureRefusesInvalidSourceIdentity`.\n142|  The standalone-entry bound (re-decode inside the entry or an\n143|  explicit pre-validated-identity contract) belongs to the\n144|  clonebundle owner or the Final leaf.\n145|- The lone-surrogate member at the shared `validText` gate (P3-ζ)\n146|  is not exercised here: this leaf owns no title/text admission\n147|  site. Deferred to the Final leaf, which owns projection\n148|  fidelity over session/event text.","final_result":true}}}
