{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c95f","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0b3c6-628c-70a3-ad39-75274b1adfea"},"sequence":778,"recorded_at":1780531400001551,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"94f324ce-ad7a-4eb7-9c54-86bfc93d2b24","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"94f324ce-ad7a-4eb7-9c54-86bfc93d2b24","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"94f324ce-ad7a-4eb7-9c54-86bfc93d2b24"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0b3c8-91ff-7660-9906-92fef35440a0"},"task_id":"01a0b3c8-91ff-7660-9906-92fef35440a0","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a0b3c8-91ff-7660-9906-92fef35440a0","chunk":"Read text file `internal/cloneproject/testdata/mutant_harness.py`.\n1|#!/usr/bin/env python3\n2|\"\"\"Narrowing-mutant harness for internal/cloneproject.\n3|\n4|Every gate ships a narrowing mutant: the gate stays present and is\n5|weakened to admit exactly one member of the class it must reject, and\n6|the named killer test must fail. A delete-only mutant proves only that\n7|the gate exists and is not accepted as evidence.\n8|\n9|Each row runs M (mutate one production file in place), R (run the\n10|scoped Go killer through the production Normalize entry over real\n11|captured bytes), V (verdict from the Go exit code plus a FAIL\n12|kill-line: KILLED iff R fails with a test failure line, SURVIVED iff\n13|R passes, ERROR for anything else — unapplied patches, build breaks,\n14|timeouts). M failures and R infrastructure errors are ERROR, never\n15|kills or survivals. The file is restored from its backup after every\n16|row, pass or fail.\n17|\n18|Rows N-native-type-token and N-protection-encrypted are the\n19|token-preserving attacks: the searched-for text still matches, but\n20|the decision changes. Their killers execute the behavioral Normalize\n21|suite over captured bytes, not a static checker.\n22|\n23|Row C-doc-comment is the harmless control: a comment-only edit that\n24|must SURVIVE, proving the harness observes test outcomes instead of\n25|hard-coding kills.\n26|\n27|Usage:\n28|  PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1 python3 internal/cloneproject/testdata/mutant_harness.py [--log-dir DIR] [MUTANT ...]\n29|\"\"\"\n30|\n31|import shutil\n32|import subprocess\n33|import sys\n34|import tempfile\n35|import time\n36|from dataclasses import dataclass\n37|from pathlib import Path\n38|\n39|REPO = Path(__file__).resolve().parents[3]\n40|PACKAGE = \"internal/cloneproject\"\n41|\n42|\n43|@dataclass(frozen=True)\n44|class Mutant:\n45|    name: str\n46|    path: str\n47|    find: str\n48|    replace: str\n49|    count: int\n50|    run: str\n51|    expect: str\n52|    note: str\n53|\n54|\n55|MUTANTS = [\n56|    Mutant(\n57|        name=\"N-unknown-kind\",\n58|        path=f\"{PACKAGE}/dispatch.go\",\n59|        find='''\\tdefault:\\n\\t\\tunit.kind = \"opaque_event\"\\n''',\n60|        replace='''\\tdefault:\\n\\t\\tunit.kind = \"opaque_event\"\\n\\t\\tif record.NativeType == \"message/smoke\" {\\n\\t\\t\\tunit.kind = \"user_message\"\\n\\t\\t}\\n''',\n61|        count=1,\n62|        run=\"TestNormalizeAlmostKnownRecordBecomesOpaqueEvent\",\n63|        expect=\"KILLED\",\n64|        note=\"Admits exactly message/smoke past the unknown-type gate into user_message; every other unknown type still projects opaque_event.\",\n65|    ),\n66|    Mutant(\n67|        name=\"N-native-type-token\",\n68|        path=f\"{PACKAGE}/dispatch.go\",\n69|        find='''\\tcase nativeMessageUser:\\n\\t\\tunit.kind = \"user_message\"\\n''',\n70|        replace='''\\tcase nativeMessageUser:\\n\\t\\tunit.kind = \"assistant_message\"\\n''',\n71|        count=1,\n72|        run=\"TestNormalizeSealsSessionShape\",\n73|        expect=\"KILLED\",\n74|        note=\"Token-preserving: the message/user label still matches but routes to assistant_message; the behavioral killer pins the kind.\",\n75|    ),\n76|    Mutant(\n77|        name=\"N-unknown-member\",\n78|        path=f\"{PACKAGE}/normalize.go\",\n79|        find='''\\t\\tif item.Class == \"unknown\" {\\n''',\n80|        replace='''\\t\\tif item.Class == \"unknown\" && item.NativeItemKey != \"store/mystery\" {\\n''',\n81|        count=1,\n82|        run=\"TestNormalizeUnknownMemberBecomesWholeMemberOpaque\",\n83|        expect=\"KILLED\",\n84|        note=\"Admits exactly store/mystery past the unknown-class gate into JSONL parsing; every other unknown member still projects whole-member opaque.\",\n85|    ),\n86|    Mutant(\n87|        name=\"N-protection-encrypted\",\n88|        path=f\"{PACKAGE}/dispatch.go\",\n89|        find='''\\tif record.Protection != \"none\" {\\n''',\n90|        replace='''\\tif record.Protection != \"none\" && record.Protection != \"encrypted\" {\\n''',\n91|        count=1,\n92|        run=\"TestNormalizeForeignEncryptedReasoningStaysOpaque\",\n93|        expect=\"KILLED\",\n94|        note=\"Token-preserving narrowing: admits exactly encrypted records past the protection gate; signed records still project opaque.\",\n95|    ),\n96|    Mutant(\n97|        name=\"N-reasoning-contradiction\",\n98|        path=f\"{PACKAGE}/dispatch.go\",\n99|        find='''\\tcase nativeReasoningCrypt, nativeReasoningSigned:\\n\\t\\twhere := \"record \" + record.MemberKey + \" line \" + itoa(record.Line)\\n\\t\\treturn invalid(\"%s declares %s with no protection\", where, record.NativeType)\\n''',\n100|        replace='''\\tcase nativeReasoningCrypt, nativeReasoningSigned:\\n\\t\\twhere := \"record \" + record.MemberKey + \" line \" + itoa(record.Line)\\n\\t\\tif record.NativeType == \"reasoning/signed\" {\\n\\t\\t\\treturn invalid(\"%s declares %s with no protection\", where, record.NativeType)\\n\\t\\t}\\n\\t\\tunit.kind = \"reasoning_summary\"\\n\\t\\tunit.visibility = \"internal\"\\n\\t\\tunit.payload = map[string]any{\"content_blocks\": []any{}, \"extensions\": map[string]any{}}\\n\\t\\treturn nil\\n''',\n101|        count=1,\n102|        run=\"TestNormalizeRefusalTable/contradictory_protection\",\n103|        expect=\"KILLED\",\n104|        note=\"Admits exactly unprotected reasoning/encrypted as reasoning_summary; unprotected reasoning/signed still refuses.\",\n105|    ),\n106|    Mutant(\n107|        name=\"N-foreign-instruction\",\n108|        path=f\"{PACKAGE}/tools.go\",\n109|        find='''\\t\\tif observation.record.Origin != \"native\" {\\n''',\n110|        replace='''\\t\\tif observation.record.Origin != \"native\" && observation.record.NativeEventID != \"evt-inst-foreign\" {\\n''',\n111|        count=1,\n112|        run=\"TestNormalizeForeignInstructionCannotChangeEffectiveSnapshot\",\n113|        expect=\"KILLED\",\n114|        note=\"Admits exactly the foreign instruction into the effective snapshot; every other foreign record stays history-only.\",\n115|    ),\n116|    Mutant(\n117|        name=\"N-foreign-payload-authority\",\n118|        path=f\"{PACKAGE}/dispatch.go\",\n119|        find='''\\tauthority := body.Authority\\n\\tif record.Origin != \"native\" {\\n\\t\\tauthority = \"low\"\\n\\t}\\n''',\n120|        replace='''\\tauthority := body.Authority\\n\\tif record.Origin != \"native\" && record.NativeEventID != \"evt-inst-foreign\" {\\n\\t\\tauthority = \"low\"\\n\\t}\\n''',\n121|        count=1,\n122|        run=\"TestNormalizeForeignInstructionCannotChangeEffectiveSnapshot\",\n123|        expect=\"KILLED\",\n124|        note=\"Admits exactly the foreign high claim into the payload authority; every other foreign instruction still pins low.\",\n125|    ),\n126|    Mutant(\n127|        name=\"N-tool-incomplete\",\n128|        path=f\"{PACKAGE}/tools.go\",\n129|        find='''\\t\\tresult, ok := seenResults[call.body.CallID]\\n\\t\\tif !ok {\\n''',\n130|        replace='''\\t\\tresult, ok := seenResults[call.body.CallID]\\n\\t\\tif !ok && call.body.CallID != \"call-7\" {\\n''',\n131|        count=1,\n132|        run=\"TestNormalizeToolMatrix/call_without_result\",\n133|        expect=\"KILLED\",\n134|        note=\"Admits exactly call-7 without its result as completed; every other incomplete call still becomes aborted history.\",\n135|    ),\n136|    Mutant(\n137|        name=\"N-tool-orphan\",\n138|        path=f\"{PACKAGE}/tools.go\",\n139|        find='''\\tfor _, result := range results {\\n\\t\\tif _, ok := seenCalls[result.body.CallID]; !ok {\\n\\t\\t\\tresolutions = append(resolutions, ToolResolution{\\n\\t\\t\\t\\tCallID:       result.body.CallID,\\n\\t\\t\\t\\tStatus:       StatusAborted,\\n\\t\\t\\t\\tResultStatus: result.body.Status,\\n\\t\\t\\t})\\n\\t\\t}\\n\\t}\\n''',\n140|        replace='''\\tfor _, result := range results {\\n\\t\\tif _, ok := seenCalls[result.body.CallID]; !ok {\\n\\t\\t\\tstatus := StatusAborted\\n\\t\\t\\tif result.body.CallID == \"call-ghost\" {\\n\\t\\t\\t\\tstatus = StatusCompleted\\n\\t\\t\\t}\\n\\t\\t\\tresolutions = append(resolutions, ToolResolution{\\n\\t\\t\\t\\tCallID:       result.body.CallID,\\n\\t\\t\\t\\tStatus:       status,\\n\\t\\t\\t\\tResultStatus: result.body.Status,\\n\\t\\t\\t})\\n\\t\\t}\\n\\t}\\n''',\n141|        count=1,\n142|        run=\"TestNormalizeToolMatrix/result_without_call\",\n143|        expect=\"KILLED\",\n144|        note=\"Admits exactly the ghost orphan result as completed; every other orphan still becomes aborted history.\",\n145|    ),\n146|    Mutant(\n147|        name=\"N-callable\",\n148|        path=f\"{PACKAGE}/tools.go\",\n149|        find='''\\t\\tif definition.body.LiveClaim {\\n\\t\\t\\twhere := \"record \" + definition.record.MemberKey + \" line \" + itoa(definition.record.Line)\\n\\t\\t\\treturn LiveSurface{}, invalid(\"%s claims live authority for historical tool definition %q\", where, definition.body.ToolName)\\n\\t\\t}\\n''',\n150|        replace='''\\t\\tif definition.body.LiveClaim && definition.body.ToolName != \"evil-tool\" {\\n\\t\\t\\twhere := \"record \" + definition.record.MemberKey + \" line \" + itoa(definition.record.Line)\\n\\t\\t\\treturn LiveSurface{}, invalid(\"%s claims live authority for historical tool definition %q\", where, definition.body.ToolName)\\n\\t\\t}\\n\\t\\tif definition.body.LiveClaim {\\n\\t\\t\\tsurface.CallableTools = append(surface.CallableTools, definition.body.ToolName)\\n\\t\\t}\\n''',\n151|        count=1,\n152|        run=\"TestNormalizeRefusalTable/live_attestation_claim\",\n153|        expect=\"KILLED\",\n154|        note=\"Admits exactly evil-tool past the live-claim refusal and registers it callable; every other live claim still refuses.\",\n155|    ),\n156|    Mutant(\n157|        name=\"N-callable-false\",\n158|        path=f\"{PACKAGE}/dispatch.go\",\n159|        find='''\\t\\t\"callable\":          false,\\n''',\n160|        replace='''\\t\\t\"callable\":          unit.record.NativeEventID == \"evt-def-1\",\\n''',\n161|        count=1,\n162|        run=\"TestNormalizeToolDefinitionNeverRegistersCallable\",\n163|        expect=\"KILLED\",\n164|        note=\"Admits exactly evt-def-1 as callable in the sealed payload; the token stays and every other definition still pins false.\",\n165|    ),\n166|    Mutant(\n167|        name=\"N-pending-aborted\",\n168|        path=f\"{PACKAGE}/tools.go\",\n169|        find='''\\t\\tif resolution.Status == StatusAborted {\\n\\t\\t\\tcontinue\\n\\t\\t}\\n''',\n170|        replace='''\\t\\tif resolution.Status == StatusAborted && resolution.CallID != \"call-7\" {\\n\\t\\t\\tcontinue\\n\\t\\t}\\n\\t\\tif resolution.CallID == \"call-7\" {\\n\\t\\t\\tsurface.PendingActions = append(surface.PendingActions, resolution.CallID)\\n\\t\\t\\tcontinue\\n\\t\\t}\\n''',\n171|        count=1,\n172|        run=\"TestNormalizeToolMatrix/call_without_result\",\n173|        expect=\"KILLED\",\n174|        note=\"Admits exactly the aborted call-7 as a pending action; every other aborted call still never pends.\",\n175|    ),\n176|    Mutant(\n177|        name=\"N-pending-completed\",\n178|        path=f\"{PACKAGE}/tools.go\",\n179|        find='''\\t\\tif liveWorkOrders[resolution.CallID] {\\n''',\n180|        replace='''\\t\\tif liveWorkOrders[resolution.CallID] || resolution.CallID == \"call-1\" {\\n''',\n181|        count=1,\n182|        run=\"TestNormalizeToolMatrix/call_with_result\",\n183|        expect=\"KILLED\",\n184|        note=\"Admits exactly the completed call-1 as pending without a live work order; every other completed call still needs one.\",\n185|    ),\n186|    Mutant(\n187|        name=\"N-live-followup\",\n188|        path=f\"{PACKAGE}/tools.go\",\n189|        find='''\\t\\tif result.body.LiveFollowup {\\n''',\n190|        replace='''\\t\\tif result.body.LiveFollowup && result.body.CallID != \"call-live\" {\\n''',\n191|        count=1,\n192|        run=\"TestNormalizeRefusalTable/live_followup_claim\",\n193|        expect=\"KILLED\",\n194|        note=\"Admits exactly the call-live followup claim; every other live followup still refuses.\",\n195|    ),\n196|    Mutant(\n197|        name=\"N-duplicate-call\",\n198|        path=f\"{PACKAGE}/tools.go\",\n199|        find='''\\t\\tif _, duplicate := seenCalls[call.body.CallID]; duplicate {\\n''',\n200|        replace='''\\t\\tif _, duplicate := seenCalls[call.body.CallID]; duplicate && call.body.CallID != \"call-dup\" {\\n''',\n201|        count=1,\n202|        run=\"TestNormalizeRefusalTable/duplicate_call_id\",\n203|        expect=\"KILLED\",\n204|        note=\"Admits exactly the duplicated call-dup ID; every other duplicate call still refuses.\",\n205|    ),\n206|    Mutant(\n207|        name=\"N-usage-target\",\n208|        path=f\"{PACKAGE}/tools.go\",\n209|        find='''\\t\\tledger.SourceInputTokens = input\\n\\t\\tledger.SourceOutputTokens = output\\n''',\n210|        replace='''\\t\\tledger.SourceInputTokens = input\\n\\t\\tledger.SourceOutputTokens = output\\n\\t\\tif observation.record.NativeEventID == \"evt-use-1\" {\\n\\t\\t\\tledger.TargetInputTokens += observation.body.InputTokens\\n\\t\\t}\\n''',\n211|        count=1,\n212|        run=\"TestNormalizeSourceUsageIsNotTargetAccounting\",\n213|        expect=\"KILLED\",\n214|        note=\"Funds the target ledger from exactly evt-use-1; every other source record still counts source-only.\",\n215|    ),\n216|    Mutant(\n217|        name=\"N-overflow-bound\",\n218|        path=f\"{PACKAGE}/overflow.go\",\n219|        find='''\\tif len(text) > maxInlineContentBytes {\\n''',\n220|        replace='''\\tif len(text) > maxInlineContentBytes+1 {\\n''',\n221|        count=1,\n222|        run=\"TestNormalizeInlineContentBoundary\",\n223|        expect=\"KILLED\",\n224|        note=\"Admits exactly 65537-byte text inline past the 64 KiB bound; 65538+ still becomes a blob reference.\",\n225|    ),\n226|    Mutant(\n227|        name=\"N-overflow-truncate\",\n228|        path=f\"{PACKAGE}/overflow.go\",\n229|        find='''\\tif len(text) > maxInlineContentBytes {\\n\\t\\tinstalled, err := installOverflow(sink, text)\\n''',\n230|        replace='''\\tif len(text) > maxInlineContentBytes {\\n\\t\\ttext = text[:maxInlineContentBytes]\\n\\t}\\n\\tif false {\\n\\t\\tinstalled, err := installOverflow(sink, text)\\n''',\n231|        count=1,\n232|        run=\"TestNormalizeInlineContentBoundary\",\n233|        expect=\"KILLED\",\n234|        note=\"Silently truncates oversized text to 64 KiB instead of installing a blob reference; the byte-exactness killer reddens.\",\n235|    ),\n236|    Mutant(\n237|        name=\"N-unstable\",\n238|        path=f\"{PACKAGE}/normalize.go\",\n239|        find='''\\tif err := clonebundle.RefuseUnstableForTarget(capture.CaptureBoundary); err != nil {\\n\\t\\treturn nil, err\\n\\t}\\n''',\n240|        replace='''\\tif err := clonebundle.RefuseUnstableForTarget(capture.CaptureBoundary); err != nil && capture.OperationID.String() != \"0198f4d1-9e60-7a11-8a31-abcdef012345\" {\\n\\t\\treturn nil, err\\n\\t}\\n''',\n241|        count=1,\n242|        run=\"TestNormalizeRefusesUnstableCapture\",\n243|        expect=\"KILLED\",\n244|        note=\"Admits exactly the fixture unstable archive to target projection; every other unstable capture still refuses.\",\n245|    ),\n246|    Mutant(\n247|        name=\"N-digest-verify\",\n248|        path=f\"{PACKAGE}/normalize.go\",\n249|        find='''\\t\\tif scalar.SHA256Digest(payload).String() != entry.BlobID.String() {\\n''',\n250|        replace='''\\t\\tif scalar.SHA256Digest(payload).String() != entry.BlobID.String() && item.NativeItemKey != \"store/session.jsonl\" {\\n''',\n251|        count=1,\n252|        run=\"TestNormalizeRefusalTable/tampered_blob\",\n253|        expect=\"KILLED\",\n254|        note=\"Skips the digest check for exactly store/session.jsonl; the tampered bytes then fail framing instead of the digest refusal.\",\n255|    ),\n256|    Mutant(\n257|        name=\"N-subagent-actor\",\n258|        path=f\"{PACKAGE}/dispatch.go\",\n259|        find='''\\t\\tif unit.record.Actor == \"main\" {\\n''',\n260|        replace='''\\t\\tif unit.record.Actor == \"main\" || unit.record.Actor == \"subagent:fetch\" {\\n''',\n261|        count=1,\n262|        run=\"TestNormalizeToolMatrix/nested_subagent_call\",\n263|        expect=\"KILLED\",\n264|        note=\"Attributes exactly the nested fetch call to main; every other non-main selector still resolves to its mapped actor.\",\n265|    ),\n266|    Mutant(\n267|        name=\"N-instruction-authority\",\n268|        path=f\"{PACKAGE}/native.go\",\n269|        find='''\\tif authority != \"high\" && authority != \"low\" {\\n''',\n270|        replace='''\\tif authority != \"high\" && authority != \"low\" && authority != \"absolute\" {\\n''',\n271|        count=1,\n272|        run=\"TestNormalizeRefusalTable/bad_instruction_authority\",\n273|        expect=\"KILLED\",\n274|        note=\"Admits exactly the absolute authority claim; every other non-high/low claim still refuses.\",\n275|    ),\n276|    Mutant(\n277|        name=\"N-definition-digest\",\n278|        path=f\"{PACKAGE}/normalize.go\",\n279|        find='''\\t\\t\\tif _, err := scalar.ParseDigest(body.DefinitionHash); err != nil {\\n''',\n280|        replace='''\\t\\t\\tif _, err := scalar.ParseDigest(body.DefinitionHash); err != nil && body.DefinitionHash != \"not-a-digest\" {\\n''',\n281|        count=1,\n282|        run=\"TestNormalizeRefusalTable/bad_definition_digest\",\n283|        expect=\"KILLED\",\n284|        note=\"Admits exactly the not-a-digest definition hash; every other malformed digest still refuses.\",\n285|    ),\n286|    Mutant(\n287|        name=\"N-parents-chain\",\n288|        path=f\"{PACKAGE}/dispatch.go\",\n289|        find='''\\t\\tparents := []string{}\\n\\t\\tif previous != nil {\\n\\t\\t\\tparents = []string{previous.String()}\\n\\t\\t}\\n''',\n290|        replace='''\\t\\tparents := []string{}\\n\\t\\tif previous != nil && index != 1 {\\n\\t\\t\\tparents = []string{previous.String()}\\n\\t\\t}\\n''',\n291|        count=1,\n292|        run=\"TestNormalizeSealsSessionShape\",\n293|        expect=\"KILLED\",\n294|        note=\"Leaves exactly ordinal 1 unparented; every other ordinal still chains to its predecessor.\",\n295|    ),\n296|    Mutant(\n297|        name=\"N-string-bound\",\n298|        path=f\"{PACKAGE}/native.go\",\n299|        find='''\\tif environ.StringLength(envelope.NativeEventID) < 1 || environ.StringLength(envelope.NativeEventID) > 512 {\\n''',\n300|        replace='''\\tif environ.StringLength(envelope.NativeEventID) < 1 || environ.StringLength(envelope.NativeEventID) > 513 {\\n''',\n301|        count=1,\n302|        run=\"TestNormalizeMultibyteStringMeasure\",\n303|        expect=\"KILLED\",\n304|        note=\"Admits exactly a 513-character native event ID; 514+ still refuses. Representative narrowing for the shared character-width rule.\",\n305|    ),\n306|    Mutant(\n307|        name=\"N-envelope-version\",\n308|        path=f\"{PACKAGE}/native.go\",\n309|        find='''\\tif envelope.Version.String() != \"1\" {\\n''',\n310|        replace='''\\tif envelope.Version.String() != \"1\" && envelope.Version.String() != \"2\" {\\n''',\n311|        count=1,\n312|        run=\"TestNormalizeRefusalTable/bad_envelope_version\",\n313|        expect=\"KILLED\",\n314|        note=\"Admits exactly envelope version 2; every other non-1 version still refuses.\",\n315|    ),\n316|    Mutant(\n317|        name=\"N-origin\",\n318|        path=f\"{PACKAGE}/native.go\",\n319|        find='''\\tif envelope.Origin != \"native\" && envelope.Origin != \"foreign\" {\\n''',\n320|        replace='''\\tif envelope.Origin != \"native\" && envelope.Origin != \"foreign\" && envelope.Origin != \"sideways\" {\\n''',\n321|        count=1,\n322|        run=\"TestNormalizeRefusalTable/bad_origin\",\n323|        expect=\"KILLED\",\n324|        note=\"Admits exactly the sideways origin; every other non-native/foreign origin still refuses.\",\n325|    ),\n326|    Mutant(\n327|        name=\"N-protection-value\",\n328|        path=f\"{PACKAGE}/native.go\",\n329|        find='''\\tif envelope.Protection != \"none\" && envelope.Protection != \"encrypted\" && envelope.Protection != \"signed\" {\\n''',\n330|        replace='''\\tif envelope.Protection != \"none\" && envelope.Protection != \"encrypted\" && envelope.Protection != \"signed\" && envelope.Protection != \"rot13\" {\\n''',\n331|        count=1,\n332|        run=\"TestNormalizeRefusalTable/bad_protection\",\n333|        expect=\"KILLED\",\n334|        note=\"Admits exactly the rot13 protection; every other out-of-vocabulary protection still refuses.\",\n335|    ),\n336|    Mutant(\n337|        name=\"N-actor-selector\",\n338|        path=f\"{PACKAGE}/native.go\",\n339|        find='''\\tname, ok := strings.CutPrefix(selector, \"subagent:\")\\n\\tif !ok || name == \"\" {\\n''',\n340|        replace='''\\tname, ok := strings.CutPrefix(selector, \"subagent:\")\\n\\tif (!ok || name == \"\") && selector != \"boss\" {\\n''',\n341|        count=1,\n342|        run=\"TestNormalizeRefusalTable/bad_actor_shape\",\n343|        expect=\"KILLED\",\n344|        note=\"Admits exactly the boss selector; every other malformed selector still refuses.\",\n345|    ),\n346|    Mutant(\n347|        name=\"N-subagent-name\",\n348|        path=f\"{PACKAGE}/native.go\",\n349|        find='''\\tif environ.StringLength(name) > 128 {\\n''',\n350|        replace='''\\tif environ.StringLength(name) > 129 {\\n''',\n351|        count=1,\n352|        run=\"TestNormalizeRefusalTable/long_subagent_name\",\n353|        expect=\"KILLED\",\n354|        note=\"Admits exactly a 129-character subagent name; 130+ still refuses.\",\n355|    ),\n356|    Mutant(\n357|        name=\"N-body-member\",\n358|        path=f\"{PACKAGE}/native.go\",\n359|        find='''\\tfor name := range members {\\n\\t\\tif !allowed[name] {\\n''',\n360|        replace='''\\tfor name := range members {\\n\\t\\tif !allowed[name] && name != \"escalate\" {\\n''',\n361|        count=1,\n362|        run=\"TestNormalizeRefusalTable/unknown_body_member\",\n363|        expect=\"KILLED\",\n364|        note=\"Admits exactly the escalate body member past the shared exact-shape gate; every other unknown member still refuses.\",\n365|    ),\n366|    Mutant(\n367|        name=\"N-blank-line\",\n368|        path=f\"{PACKAGE}/native.go\",\n369|        find='''\\t\\tif len(raw) == 0 {\\n\\t\\t\\treturn nil, invalid(\"record %s line %d is empty\", memberKey, number)\\n\\t\\t}\\n''',\n370|        replace='''\\t\\tif len(raw) == 0 && number != 2 {\\n\\t\\t\\treturn nil, invalid(\"record %s line %d is empty\", memberKey, number)\\n\\t\\t}\\n''',\n371|        count=1,\n372|        run=\"TestNormalizeRefusalTable/blank_line\",\n373|        expect=\"KILLED\",\n374|        note=\"Admits exactly a blank line 2; a blank line anywhere else still refuses.\",\n375|    ),\n376|    Mutant(\n377|        name=\"N-malformed-json\",\n378|        path=f\"{PACKAGE}/native.go\",\n379|        find='''\\tvar members map[string]json.RawMessage\\n\\tif err := decoder.Decode(&members); err != nil {\\n\\t\\treturn NativeRecord{}, invalid(\"%s is not a JSON object: %v\", where(), err)\\n\\t}\\n''',\n380|        replace='''\\tvar members map[string]json.RawMessage\\n\\tif err := decoder.Decode(&members); err != nil && string(raw) != \"{not-json\" {\\n\\t\\treturn NativeRecord{}, invalid(\"%s is not a JSON object: %v\", where(), err)\\n\\t}\\n''',\n381|        count=1,\n382|        run=\"TestNormalizeRefusalTable/malformed_json_line\",\n383|        expect=\"KILLED\",\n384|        note=\"Admits exactly the killer's malformed line past the JSON gate into the envelope gate; every other malformed line still refuses at the JSON gate.\",\n385|    ),\n386|    Mutant(\n387|        name=\"N-usage-number\",\n388|        path=f\"{PACKAGE}/native.go\",\n389|        find='''\\tfor i := 0; i < len(text); i++ {\\n\\t\\tif text[i] < '0' || text[i] > '9' {\\n\\t\\t\\treturn 0, invalid(\"%s body member %q is not a uint53\", where, name)\\n\\t\\t}\\n\\t}\\n''',\n390|        replace='''\\tfor i := 0; i < len(text); i++ {\\n\\t\\tif text[i] < '0' || text[i] > '9' {\\n\\t\\t\\tif text == \"1.5\" {\\n\\t\\t\\t\\tcontinue\\n\\t\\t\\t}\\n\\t\\t\\treturn 0, invalid(\"%s body member %q is not a uint53\", where, name)\\n\\t\\t}\\n\\t}\\n''',\n391|        count=1,\n392|        run=\"TestNormalizeRefusalTable/fractional_usage\",\n393|        expect=\"KILLED\",\n394|        note=\"Admits exactly 1.5 past the digit gate into the range gate; every other non-digit literal still refuses at the digit gate.\",\n395|    ),\n396|    Mutant(\n397|        name=\"N-directive-count\",\n398|        path=f\"{PACKAGE}/native.go\",\n399|        find='''\\tif len(directives) > 1024 {\\n''',\n400|        replace='''\\tif len(directives) > 1025 {\\n''',\n401|        count=1,\n402|        run=\"TestNormalizeRefusalTable/too_many_directives\",\n403|        expect=\"KILLED\",\n404|        note=\"Admits exactly 1025 directives; 1026+ still refuses.\",\n405|    ),\n406|    Mutant(\n407|        name=\"N-usage-overflow\",\n408|        path=f\"{PACKAGE}/tools.go\",\n409|        find='''\\t\\tif input < ledger.SourceInputTokens || input > maxUint53 {\\n''',\n410|        replace='''\\t\\tif input < ledger.SourceInputTokens || input > maxUint53+1 {\\n''',\n411|        count=1,\n412|        run=\"TestNormalizeRefusalTable/usage_ledger_overflow\",\n413|        expect=\"KILLED\",\n414|        note=\"Admits exactly the 2^53 input total; anything larger still refuses instead of wrapping.\",\n415|    ),\n416|    Mutant(\n417|        name=\"N-duplicate-result\",\n418|        path=f\"{PACKAGE}/tools.go\",\n419|        find='''\\t\\tif _, duplicate := seenResults[result.body.CallID]; duplicate {\\n''',\n420|        replace='''\\t\\tif _, duplicate := seenResults[result.body.CallID]; duplicate && result.body.CallID != \"call-r\" {\\n''',\n421|        count=1,\n422|        run=\"TestNormalizeRefusalTable/duplicate_result_id\",\n423|        expect=\"KILLED\",\n424|        note=\"Admits exactly the duplicated call-r result; every other duplicate result still refuses.\",\n425|    ),\n426|    Mutant(\n427|        name=\"N-empty-projection\",\n428|        path=f\"{PACKAGE}/normalize.go\",\n429|        find='''\\tif len(plan.units) == 0 {\\n\\t\\treturn nil, invalid(\"projection holds no events\")\\n\\t}\\n''',\n430|        replace='''\\tif len(plan.units) < 0 {\\n\\t\\treturn nil, invalid(\"projection holds no events\")\\n\\t}\\n''',\n431|        count=1,\n432|        run=\"TestNormalizeRefusalTable/empty_projection\",\n433|        expect=\"KILLED\",\n434|        note=\"Admits the empty projection past the unit gate into the session builder; the single-member empty class still refuses at its own gate.\",\n435|    ),\n436|    Mutant(\n437|        name=\"N-missing-blob\",\n438|        path=f\"{PACKAGE}/normalize.go\",\n439|        find='''\\t\\tpayload, err := plan.request.Fetch(entry.BlobID.String())\\n\\t\\tif err != nil {\\n''',\n440|        replace='''\\t\\tpayload, err := plan.request.Fetch(entry.BlobID.String())\\n\\t\\tif err != nil && item.NativeItemKey != \"store/session.jsonl\" {\\n''',\n441|        count=1,\n442|        run=\"TestNormalizeRefusalTable/missing_blob\",\n443|        expect=\"KILLED\",\n444|        note=\"Admits exactly the missing session blob past the fetch gate into the size gate; every other missing blob still refuses at the fetch gate.\",\n445|    ),\n446|    Mutant(\n447|        name=\"N-manifest-link\",\n448|        path=f\"{PACKAGE}/normalize.go\",\n449|        find='''\\tif raw.ManifestID.String() != capture.SourceRawObjectManifest.String() {\\n''',\n450|        replace='''\\tif raw.ManifestID.String() != capture.SourceRawObjectManifest.String() && capture.OperationID.String() != \"0198f4d1-9e60-7a11-8a31-abcdef012345\" {\\n''',\n451|        count=1,\n452|        run=\"TestNormalizeRefusalTable/manifest_closure_drift\",\n453|        expect=\"KILLED\",\n454|        note=\"Admits exactly the fixture mismatched pair past the ID link; every other mismatched pair still refuses.\",\n455|    ),\n456|    Mutant(\n457|        name=\"N-env-drift\",\n458|        path=f\"{PACKAGE}/normalize.go\",\n459|        find='''\\tif !bytes.Equal(rawCanonical, capturedCanonical) {\\n''',\n460|        replace='''\\tif len(rawCanonical) < 8 || len(capturedCanonical) < 8 || !bytes.Equal(rawCanonical[:8], capturedCanonical[:8]) {\\n''',\n461|        count=1,\n462|        run=\"TestNormalizeRefusesEnvironmentDrift\",\n463|        expect=\"KILLED\",\n464|        note=\"Compares only the first 8 bytes, admitting exactly late-drifting tuples past the drift gate; any early drift still refuses.\",\n465|    ),\n466|    Mutant(\n467|        name=\"N-actor-unmapped-fallback\",\n468|        path=f\"{PACKAGE}/dispatch.go\",\n469|        find='''\\t\\tif _, ok := plan.extraActors[selector]; !ok {\\n\\t\\t\\treturn invalid(\"projection references actor %q with no mapped UUID\", selector)\\n\\t\\t}\\n''',\n470|        replace='''\\t\\tif _, ok := plan.extraActors[selector]; !ok && selector != \"subagent:stray\" {\\n\\t\\t\\treturn invalid(\"projection references actor %q with no mapped UUID\", selector)\\n\\t\\t}\\n''',\n471|        count=1,\n472|        run=\"TestNormalizeRefusalTable/unmapped_actor\",\n473|        expect=\"KILLED\",\n474|        note=\"Admits exactly the stray selector past the actor pre-check into the resolving layer, which refuses with its own message; every other unmapped selector still refuses at the pre-check.\",\n475|    ),\n476|    Mutant(\n477|        name=\"N-actor-unreferenced\",\n478|        path=f\"{PACKAGE}/dispatch.go\",\n479|        find='''\\tfor selector := range plan.extraActors {\\n\\t\\tif !referenced[selector] {\\n\\t\\t\\treturn invalid(\"projection maps actor %q with no referencing record\", selector)\\n\\t\\t}\\n\\t}\\n''',\n480|        replace='''\\tfor selector := range plan.extraActors {\\n\\t\\tif !referenced[selector] && selector != \"subagent:idle\" {\\n\\t\\t\\treturn invalid(\"projection maps actor %q with no referencing record\", selector)\\n\\t\\t}\\n\\t}\\n''',\n481|        count=1,\n482|        run=\"TestNormalizeRefusalTable/unmapped_extra_actor\",\n483|        expect=\"KILLED\",\n484|        note=\"Admits exactly the idle mapping without a referencing record; every other unreferenced mapping still refuses.\",\n485|    ),\n486|    Mutant(\n487|        name=\"N-main-in-map\",\n488|        path=f\"{PACKAGE}/normalize.go\",\n489|        find='''\\t\\tif selector == \"main\" {\\n\\t\\t\\treturn nil, invalid(\"projection actor map carries main, which is request.MainActorID\")\\n\\t\\t}\\n''',\n490|        replace='''\\t\\tif selector == \"main\" && value != \"0198f4d1-9e60-7a88-81a8-123456789abc\" {\\n\\t\\t\\treturn nil, invalid(\"projection actor map carries main, which is request.MainActorID\")\\n\\t\\t}\\n''',\n491|        count=1,\n492|        run=\"TestNormalizeRefusalTable/main_actor_in_map\",\n493|        expect=\"KILLED\",\n494|        note=\"Admits exactly the killer's main mapping; every other main mapping still refuses.\",\n495|    ),\n496|    Mutant(\n497|        name=\"N-protection-signed\",\n498|        path=f\"{PACKAGE}/dispatch.go\",\n499|        find='''\\tif record.Protection != \"none\" {\\n''',\n500|        replace='''\\tif record.Protection != \"none\" && record.Protection != \"signed\" {\\n''',\n(more lines below)","final_result":true}}}
