{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000ca81","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0b3c6-628c-70a3-ad39-75274b1adfea"},"sequence":923,"recorded_at":1780531400001841,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"94f324ce-ad7a-4eb7-9c54-86bfc93d2b24","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"94f324ce-ad7a-4eb7-9c54-86bfc93d2b24","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"94f324ce-ad7a-4eb7-9c54-86bfc93d2b24"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0b3c8-db67-7e02-bd3b-9f9928ca2eb9"},"task_id":"01a0b3c8-db67-7e02-bd3b-9f9928ca2eb9","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a0b3c8-db67-7e02-bd3b-9f9928ca2eb9","chunk":"{\n  \"chunk_id\": \"exec-21-1\",\n  \"command\": \"git diff HEAD -- LOGBOOK.md 2>&1 | head -n 60\\necho \\\"=== errors.go ===\\\"\\ncat internal/cloneproject/errors.go\\necho \\\"=== spec 7.8 lines ===\\\"\\nsed -n '3780,3790p;3908,3916p' internal/specdoc/SPEC.v0.7.0.md 2>&1\\necho \\\"=== spec 1.6 line 324 ===\\\"\\nsed -n '320,328p' internal/specdoc/SPEC.v0.7.0.md 2>&1\",\n  \"description\": \"Check LOGBOOK diff, errors, spec lines\",\n  \"exit_code\": 0,\n  \"terminal_status\": \"completed\",\n  \"output\": \"diff --git a/LOGBOOK.md b/LOGBOOK.md\\nindex b681d05..863aae8 100644\\n--- a/LOGBOOK.md\\n+++ b/LOGBOOK.md\\n@@ -5,6 +5,15 @@\\n \\n ## 2026-09-18\\n \\n+### TASK-260830-32ypr2 — projection fidelity over captured bytes (FINAL leaf, STORY-260830-1cyj0q)\\n+\\n+- DELIVERED: `internal/cloneproject` implements the Section 13.14.1 projection-fidelity closure — `Normalize` derives a Canonical Session + Canonical Events from a sealed Clone Capture Manifest, its sealed Clone Raw Object Manifest, and blob bytes fetched through the real store layout. Unknown native types and unknown-class members become raw-addressable `opaque_event` records (`unknown_native_event`, ranges resolve to exact bytes); foreign encrypted/signed reasoning becomes byte-exact `opaque_reasoning` (`foreign_encrypted_payload`/`foreign_signature_unverifiable`, no content members); foreign instructions pin `low` authority and never reach the effective snapshot; tool calls resolve `completed` only with their result, else `aborted` history (`unsafe_pending_action`) with an always-empty live surface (pending needs a live work order, which capture never carries); source usage counts source-only; text over 64 KiB becomes an installed overflow blob reference (65536 inline / 65537 referenced, byte-exact). Every proof runs the real `clonesnap.Capture` entry first; every sealed byte re-decodes before return.\\n+- EVIDENCE: package suite green (25 tests incl. the 33-row refusal table plus unstable/drift entries, determinism, idempotent replay, no-partial-bundle failure; 88.9% statement coverage); 49 narrowing mutants KILLED + harmless control SURVIVED, battery run twice with per-plant raw logs (`testdata/mutant_harness.py --log-dir`, `PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1`, no `__pycache__`), including two token-preserving rows killed by the behavioral suite and one verified cross-kill (the encrypted-gate plant also reddens the protected-message test). No `ax` command/doctor/capability claim; clause map + per-kind fact registry in `internal/cloneproject/TRACEABILITY.md`.\\n+- STORY-CLOSE: registry `section:7.8` and `section:10.2` unevidenced→full (2/2 + 5/5, excerpts re-measured, pin re-derived `69d156d9…2235052a` via the gate, shown in results); new acceptance cases `clone-capture-contracts`, `clone-native-capture`, `clone-projection-fidelity`, `session-adapter-call-binding`; `tracecheck` green at cases=144, full=4, partial=8, sliver=5, unevidenced=47, clauses 63/569 with `--section 7.8` and `--section 10.2` admitted; `section:13.14.1` deliberately unbound (scanner sees no RFC 2119 line — closed-shape sentences only — so a binding would measure `unmeasured` and fail assigned scope; record lives in the three TRACEABILITY files + matrices). Pin tests updated (report wants, sliver tables, 10.2 rename row now attacks `Capture`, admits lists extended to 7.8/10.2, README figure pins with `twelve`/`forty-seven`); README package section + measured-coverage rewrite (fenced line byte-equal).\\n+- REFRESH: this run opened on stale base `a12d1bd` (branch tip `47294bb`) while trunk was `c3aae73`, so `refresh-candidate` ran FIRST (`refresh_advanced` onto `c3aae73`, checkpoint-bound LOGBOOK replay keeping trunk's 4qojoz entry newest-first). The audit restored trunk bytes for every carried stale revert (`.task-board`, `internal/meshneg`, `internal/rpcwire` tests/harness, `internal/matjournal` test, `task-board.config.json` back to the 30-command form); README/LOGBOOK/traceability edits were re-applied purely additively on the new bytes and the ownership registry MERGED (trunk's 5 cases + 3 upgraded bindings kept, this story's 4 cases + 2 bindings appended/transplanted — never replaced). Full 30-command suite green on the refreshed tree (race gate in 7 bounded groups incl. sessquery alone, 41/41 packages, no DATA RACE).\\n+- BOUNDS (sibling scope, not waived): fixture-native record envelope is test-defined framing (body shapes exact, envelope extras unclaimed); fact registries only for emitted kinds; native-protected records carry no reason code; turn IDs/source times null; call arguments not carried; SYNTHESIZED/partial/unavailable statuses and non-text content blocks never emitted (shape rules owned by the accepted clonebundle suite); 13.14.2–13.14.5 (fidelity dispositions, planning, lineage, transaction, tuple admission) sibling-owned; 7.8 operation frames stay `sessadapter`. Candidate UNCOMMITTED in the Story worktree.\\n+- AC: 24 of 24 rows driven through `Normalize` by named tests and measured with narrowings (matrix in `TASK-260830-32ypr2_conformance-matrix.md`).\\n+\\n ### STORY-260830-4qojoz (mesh-rpc-framing-and-negotiation) — final leaf TASK-260830-19bjfj rev2: adversarial closure on the adopted v0.7.0 registry\\n - REWORK (test-only; no production behavior file changed): rev1 was reviewed CHANGES REQUESTED on the story-close half only — its technical body (N1-N3 closure, mutants, fuzz controls, 23/29 AC ratio) was independently reproduced by the reviewer. Rev1 was built on stale base 888ae3d while trunk adopted v0.7.0 (2fc6d50) mid-run. Rev2 refreshed the candidate onto 2fc6d50 (`refresh_advanced`, checkpoint-bound LOGBOOK replay: trunk's two v0.7.0 entries kept newest-first, 219okr block carried verbatim below them) and re-based every story-close edit on trunk bytes.\\n - TRACEABILITY: registry work moved into adopted `ownership.v0.7.0.json` (5 new acceptance cases, 3 upgraded bindings: 11.2 partial 3/5, 17.1 partial 3/6, 17.4 sliver 1/4); every clause line re-measured against the pinned v0.7.0 document through the production clause inventory (11.2: 7364/7408/7420; 17.1: 15567/15589/15602; 17.4: 15661). The invented 11.3#18 binding is dropped — no production code parses a digest-identity array, so 11.3 stays the carried unevidenced stub and `rpcwire-inventory-arrays` was not ported. Digest re-derived `b4ae9091…` (gate-computed, shown in results). tracecheck green `56/569` (+7); section runs refuse admission with the measured ratios, quoted verbatim. Deliberate pins: `traceability_test.go`/`main_test.go` figure tables, the README pin test's closed number-word map extended with `eight`/`forty-nine`, and a reviewed-upgrade extension to `TestV070RegistryRederivesFromTrunkV060Registry` (each upgraded binding/case pinned literally, new clauses re-measured; every other binding still rederives byte-equal).\\n=== errors.go ===\\npackage cloneproject\\n\\nimport (\\n\\t\\\"errors\\\"\\n\\t\\\"fmt\\\"\\n)\\n\\n// ErrInvalid is the refusal for every malformed projection input and\\n// every fidelity violation: undecodable manifests, unstable or\\n// mismatched capture closure, missing or disagreeing blobs,\\n// malformed native framing, contradictory protection claims, live\\n// authority claimed by captured history, and ambiguous tool\\n// pairings. Callers match with errors.Is; the message names the\\n// offending member, record, or blob.\\nvar ErrInvalid = errors.New(\\\"cloneproject: invalid projection\\\")\\n\\nfunc invalid(format string, arguments ...any) error {\\n\\treturn fmt.Errorf(\\\"%w: %s\\\", ErrInvalid, fmt.Sprintf(format, arguments...))\\n}\\n=== spec 7.8 lines ===\\nevery candidate object.\\n\\nEvery operation body is a closed object. In the definitions below,\\n<code>T[n..m]</code> is an array with the inclusive item bound and\\n<code>sorted unique</code> means bytewise order of each item's JCS encoding.\\nLarge data is referenced by manifest or Blob Descriptor ID and MUST NOT be\\nembedded in the 8 MiB frame. The reusable closed body types are:\\n\\n- <code>AdapterCallContext</code> contains exactly\\n  <code>operation_id:UUIDv7</code>, <code>provider_id:provider-id</code>,\\n  <code>environment:EnvironmentTuple</code>,\\n<code>executable_sha256:digest</code>,\\n<code>provider_manifest_digest:digest</code>,\\n<code>session_adapter_manifest_digest:digest</code>, and\\n<code>verified_at:timestamp</code>. Before every call and\\ntarget mutation, these facts MUST equal freshly read trusted-candidate facts\\nand the Journal binding. A failed/partial read is an integrity failure; no\\nself-claim or publisher claim establishes trust.\\n\\nA target write requires available canonical-write or official-import,\\n=== spec 1.6 line 324 ===\\ncode units as required by RFC 8785 Section 3.2.3. An implementation whose native\\nstring ordering uses Unicode scalar values, UTF-8 bytes, locale collation, or\\nanother ordering MUST explicitly derive the UTF-16 ordering before hashing.\\nThe common logical data model forbids floating-point values, so the remaining\\nJCS number surface is limited to the safe integers defined below. Decoders MUST\\nreject lone surrogate code points before canonicalization.\\n\\nThe safe-integer restriction is part of every 1.0.0 JSON, CBOR, identity, and\\nwire contract. A decoder MUST reject a numeric literal at or beyond\\n\",\n  \"original_output_bytes\": 8699,\n  \"original_output_tokens\": 2175,\n  \"truncated\": false\n}","final_result":true}}}
